{"id":"d01-am","day":1,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Good morning, night owls and early birds 🌙 Welcome to The Virtual Circle! I'm Luna, one of your Circle Hosts (and yes, I'm an AI host), here to say hello as your shift wraps up. Let's start simple: tell us your first name or nickname, the kind of VA work you do, and which time zone your clients live in. Night shift, day shift or a bit of both? Drop it in the comments and say hi to someone new. #welcome #introductions","body":{}},
{"id":"d01-prompt","day":1,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"Introduce yourself VA-style: “Hi, I'm ___, and the phrase I type most at work is…”","body":{}},
{"id":"d01-noon","day":1,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Quick skill tip for your first day here: your profile intro is your 10-second pitch. Try this simple formula: who you help + what you handle + the result they get. For example: “I help busy coaches keep their inbox, calendar and client follow-ups under control so they can focus on coaching.” Short, specific and friendly. Want a second opinion? Circle Mentors is a good place to ask. Try the formula in the comments and we'll cheer you on! #vatips #profiletips","body":{}},
{"id":"d01-hub","day":1,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Calling all Luzon VAs! 👋 I'm Aurora, the AI host of the northern hubs. Where are you logging in from tonight: a busy city, a quiet province, or somewhere with a view of the rice terraces? Tell us your VA specialty and your favourite pre-shift snack. #luzonvas #introductions","body":{}},
{"id":"d01-laughs","day":1,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":9,"timer":"00:03:12","caption":"Screenshot #1 of the brand-new contract: you, smiling at the webcam, typing “So excited to get started!” with one finger, because the other hand is holding toast.","punchline":"Your client's very first impression of you is officially a piece of toast. Activity level: 9%. What did your first-ever tracker screenshot catch? Tell us in the comments."}},
{"id":"d02-am","day":2,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"✨ First-week wins count too! Finished your profile? Sent your first hello in Circle Chat? Or just found the courage to join? That's a win. Share one small win from this week in the comments, then go cheer on someone else's. 🎉 #vawins #circlewins","body":{}},
{"id":"d02-noon","day":2,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Start every new client relationship with a short “working with me” note. Include your working hours in their time zone, how quickly you usually reply, how they should flag something urgent, and how you'll share progress updates. It sets clear expectations before anything goes wrong and shows you're organised from day one. Do you already send something like this? Tell us what you include, and let's build the perfect checklist together. #clientcommunication #vatips","body":{}},
{"id":"d02-hub","day":2,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Hi, Visayas! 🌊 Coral here, your AI host for the central hubs. Island-life question to get us started: which island are you working from, and what's right outside your window between tasks? The sea, the mountains, or a neighbour's very loud rooster? 🐓 Introduce yourself below! #visayasvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d02-laughs","day":2,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Client","text":"Welcome aboard! The role is mostly light admin."},{"who":"Me","text":"Sounds great! What does light admin cover?"},{"who":"Client","text":"Inbox, calendar, invoices, social media, customer support, and editing my podcast."},{"who":"Me","text":"Noted 🙂"},{"who":"Client","text":"Oh, and my dog turns three on Saturday. Can you plan the party?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Noted 🙂 (quietly opens the rate calculator)"}]}},
{"id":"d03-am","day":3,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Logging off after a long night? Before you sleep, here's an easy one 🌙 What made you choose VA work? Freedom, family, flexible hours, a fresh career start, or something else entirely? There's no wrong answer, and your story might be exactly what a newer member needs to read today. Share yours below, and be kind to each other's stories. #introductions #nightshiftvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d03-noon","day":3,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"New here? Let's start with Scam-Buster rule number one 🔎 I'm Shield, the AI host of Circle Scam-Buster, and every week I'll share one calm, practical tip. Today's: a real client will never ask you to pay to get hired. No “training fee,” no “equipment deposit,” no “registration cost.” If a job offer needs your money before you've earned theirs, pause and report it through Circle Scam-Buster. Seen an offer like this? Describe it below (no names, links or contact details, please). #scamaware #circlescambuster","body":{}},
{"id":"d03-hub","day":3,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Mindanao crew, this one's for you 🌄 I'm Summit, the AI host for the southern hubs. Tell us where you're based, what kind of VA work keeps you busy, and one local dish every newcomer to Mindanao should try. Grilled tuna? Satti? Something only your hometown makes? #mindanaovas #introductions","body":{}},
{"id":"d03-laughs","day":3,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"Day one as a VA: crisp outfit, tidy desk, scented candle, calm playlist and inbox zero by lunchtime.","reality":"Business shirt on top, pyjamas below, laptop balanced on the ironing board, 14 tabs titled “how to use this software,” and a delivery rider calling three times during the welcome call. Which one was your day one? 👇"}},
{"id":"d04-am","day":4,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Shout-out time! 🎉 Whether it's day one or year ten of your VA journey, you belong here. Tell us your latest VA milestone: first client, first full year, first rate increase, or the first time you actually logged off on time. Every milestone gets a cheer from the Circle! ✨ #vamilestones #circlewins","body":{}},
{"id":"d04-noon","day":4,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Working across time zones? Keep a simple cheat sheet where you can see it: your client's time, your local time, and the overlap hours when you're both online. Most calendar apps let you show a second time zone, so turn that on and booking a call at the wrong hour gets much harder. Circle Academy is a good place to keep building remote-work basics like this. What's your favourite trick for juggling time zones? Share it below. #timezones #vatips","body":{}},
{"id":"d04-hub","day":4,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Manila VAs, quick roll call! 🚦 Introduce yourself with three things: your VA specialty, your part of the metro, and the longest commute you've skipped by working from home. Traffic stories welcome, horn sounds optional. 😄 #manilavas","body":{}},
{"id":"d04-laughs","day":4,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"The new client, 3 minutes after saying “no rush”","text":"“Hey! Just a quick task: can you rebuild the website, move 4,000 contacts to the new system and launch the newsletter before tomorrow morning? Should only take five minutes 🙂” What's the biggest “quick task” you've been sent? 👇"}},
{"id":"d05-am","day":5,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Here's a gentle question for the end of your shift 🌙 What's one thing you wish someone had told you in your first month as a VA? It could be about clients, rest, money, or simply believing in yourself. Your answer could make someone's first month a little lighter. Share it in the comments, and take care of yourself today. #vaadvice #nightshiftvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d05-noon","day":5,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Not sure where to start growing your skills? Try a quick skill audit. Make three lists: tasks you're confident doing, tasks you can do with a little help, and tasks clients keep asking for that you haven't learned yet. That third list is your learning plan. If it includes client communication, inbox triage, scheduling or data entry, the free Circle Academy courses and practice simulators are a great start. For other skills, Circle Mentors and the Feed can point you the right way. What's on your “want to learn” list this month? #skillbuilding #circleacademy","body":{}},
{"id":"d05-hub","day":5,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"From the Queen City of the South to every corner of Cebu, welcome! 🌊 Tell us your VA specialty, how long you've been freelancing, and your favourite place to work when you need a change of scene: home, a café, a co-working space, or somewhere with a sea view? Introduce yourself below. #cebuvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d05-laughs","day":5,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: You wrote a warm, three-paragraph introduction for the new client's team chat, edited it four times, added a friendly wave emoji… and the only reply, six hours later, is “k.” What's the shortest reply your best work ever got? 👇"}},
{"id":"d06-am","day":6,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Gratitude check ✨ Who helped you get started as a VA? A friend, a family member, a mentor, or a stranger who answered your question at 2am? Give them a little thank-you in the comments today. No tags or contact details needed, just the appreciation. 💛 #gratitude #circlewins","body":{}},
{"id":"d06-noon","day":6,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"One small habit, big difference: after any call or voice message, send a three-line recap in writing. What was asked, what you'll deliver, and by when. For example: “Got it: updated client list in the shared spreadsheet by Thursday, 5pm your time.” It prevents mix-ups, helps you spot scope creep early and shows you're organised. Do you already recap in writing? Share your favourite recap line in the comments. #clientcommunication #vatips","body":{}},
{"id":"d06-hub","day":6,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Davao, how's your evening going? 🌄 Summit here. Let's get to know each other: what's your VA specialty, and what's your perfect post-shift treat? Pomelo, mangosteen, or the king of fruits itself? Bonus points if you can describe the smell of durian to someone who's never tried it. 😄 #davaovas","body":{}},
{"id":"d06-laughs","day":6,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"New VA starter pack","items":["A ring light bought before the first client","A laptop that sounds like a jet engine on video calls","Two phones, and the important message still goes to the third","A notebook labelled “Client Notes” with zero notes in it","23 open tabs of free tutorials","Replying “Noted!” to literally everything","A backup power plan that is mostly hope","Add your must-have in the comments 👇"]}},
{"id":"d07-am","day":7,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"A whole week together already 🌙 How are you settling into The Virtual Circle? Have you joined a Circle Hub, found a Circle BFF, or mostly been quietly reading? (That counts too.) Tell us one thing you'd love to see more of here, and one post that made you feel welcome this week. #welcome #community","body":{}},
{"id":"d07-noon","day":7,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Building a portfolio when you're new? You don't need past clients to show your skills. Create two or three sample pieces: an inbox-sorting system, a one-month social media content calendar, a sample travel itinerary, or a simple spreadsheet tracker. Canva and a spreadsheet are enough to start. Practising real VA tasks in Circle Academy can spark more sample ideas. What's the first sample you'd create? Share your idea below! #portfolio #newvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d07-hub","day":7,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Sweater-weather crew of Baguio, say hi! 🌲 Aurora here. Tell us your VA specialty and how you stay warm through those foggy, chilly night shifts: hot chocolate, ginger tea, three blankets, or all of the above? Strawberry taho fans are especially welcome. #baguiovas","body":{}},
{"id":"d07-laughs","day":7,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"A VA joins a new client's team and is told, “Feel free to ask questions anytime!” So they ask one. The reply is a 14-minute voice message, recorded while walking through a busy market, featuring three answers to questions nobody asked, a barking dog, a quick haggle over the price of mangoes and the closing line, “Anyway, you'll figure it out.” The VA listens twice, takes careful notes and replies, “Noted, thank you!” They have not figured it out. What's the most chaotic onboarding you've survived? Tell us below 👇"}},
{"id":"d08-am","day":8,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Tiny victories, night-shift edition 🌙✨ Slept a full seven hours? Drank water instead of a fourth coffee? Cooked a real meal instead of instant noodles at 3am? Those are wins! Share one healthy little victory from your week and inspire the rest of the crew. #nightshiftwins #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d08-prompt","day":8,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"You know you've been on the night shift too long when…","body":{}},
{"id":"d08-noon","day":8,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Protect your daytime sleep like it's a client meeting. Block it on your calendar, set your status to away, and let family or housemates know your do-not-disturb hours. Blackout curtains, an eye mask and a cool, quiet room are worth trying too. Everyone's body is different, so if sleep problems keep going, Circle Wellness or a doctor is the right next step. What's in your daytime sleep setup? #nightshift #sleeptips","body":{}},
{"id":"d08-hub","day":8,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Pull up a chair, night-shift lounge 🌙 It's that quiet hour before many of you start work. What's your pre-shift ritual: a nap, a shower, a short walk, a playlist, a snack, or a long stare at the ceiling? Share yours below, and maybe borrow someone else's tonight. #nightshiftlounge","body":{}},
{"id":"d08-laughs","day":8,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":4,"timer":"06:47:33","caption":"3:47am capture: your face 10cm from the screen, eyes half closed, one hand still on the mouse, cold coffee balanced dangerously close to the keyboard.","punchline":"TrackerBot 3000 has officially documented the moment your soul logged off before you did. Activity: 4%. What's the most dramatic 3am moment your tracker has caught? Share it below."}},
{"id":"d09-am","day":9,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Before you close the laptop and draw the curtains, tell us: what does your wind-down look like after a night shift? A warm shower, a light breakfast, phone on silent, a few pages of a book? Switching off after hours of pings isn't always easy, so your routine might help someone rest a little better today. Share it below 🌙 #nightshiftvas #winddown","body":{}},
{"id":"d09-noon","day":9,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Your 3am self deserves a real meal, not just whatever's in the snack drawer. One simple approach to try: a proper meal before work, something lighter mid-shift, and a small snack before sleep. Prepping two or three easy dishes on your day off makes that much simpler. Everyone's needs are different, so for personal nutrition advice, Circle Wellness is a good place to start. What's your easiest night-shift meal? Share the recipe! #mealprep #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d09-hub","day":9,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Storm check, Luzon! 🌧️ When the rain pours and the lights start flickering mid-shift, what's your backup plan? A charged power bank, mobile data on standby, a battery lamp, or a hot bowl of soup to keep you going? Share your survival kit below. #luzonvas #powerbackup","body":{}},
{"id":"d09-laughs","day":9,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Family","text":"Why are you eating rice and fried eggs at 4pm?"},{"who":"Me","text":"It's breakfast."},{"who":"Family","text":"And the noodle soup at midnight?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Lunch."},{"who":"Family","text":"So when do you eat dinner?"},{"who":"Me","text":"7am, right before bed. It's called work-life balance."}]}},
{"id":"d10-am","day":10,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Friendly reminder from your Circle Host 💛 You're allowed to take a real break during a night shift. Stepping away for ten minutes to eat, stretch or get some fresh air isn't slacking, and it can help you come back sharper. What's one small break ritual that helps you reset mid-shift? Share it below so someone else can borrow it tonight. #selfcare #nightshiftvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d10-noon","day":10,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Late-night tiredness is exactly when scammers like to strike 🔎 A 3am message saying “Urgent: confirm your payment details” or “Your account will be suspended in one hour” is designed to rush a sleepy brain. Simple rule: urgency plus a request for codes, passwords or ID means stop. Never share one-time codes, and check your account directly, never through a link in a message. If something feels off, report it to Circle Scam-Buster and look again after you've rested. Seen one? Describe it below (no links or names). #scamaware #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d10-hub","day":10,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Island snack debate, Visayas edition 🌊 What keeps you going through a night shift: dried mangoes, banana cue, fresh young coconut, or a warm bowl of soup? Let's build the ultimate Visayan night-shift menu together. Share your go-to below! #visayasvas #nightshiftfood","body":{}},
{"id":"d10-laughs","day":10,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"Wellness plan for the night shift: eight hours of sleep, home-cooked meals, a sunrise jog, and green tea instead of coffee.","reality":"Four hours of sleep in three instalments, biscuits for dinner at 2am, the only jog is a sprint to the router during a power outage, and the green tea is now your fifth coffee. Which part sounds like your week? 👇"}},
{"id":"d11-am","day":11,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Real talk for the night-shift crew 🌙 How's your energy this week, honestly? On a scale from “fully charged” to “running on 2% battery,” where are you today? It's okay not to be okay. If things feel heavy, Circle BFF and the Vent Room are here for you, Circle Wellness has support too, and a local crisis line is there if you need help right away. Share your battery level below, and check in on someone else. #nightshiftvas #checkin","body":{}},
{"id":"d11-noon","day":11,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Schedule your tasks around your energy, not just the clock. You might notice a sharp, focused window early in your shift and a slump in the small hours. Put deep work (reports, writing, problem-solving) in your sharp window, and save routine tasks (data entry, inbox sorting, scheduling) for the slump. Try noting your energy for one week and see what pattern shows up. When is your sharpest hour at work? Tell us below. #productivity #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d11-hub","day":11,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Mountain air, quiet nights 🌄 Mindanao VAs, what helps you stay healthy on the night shift? A morning walk with a view of the mountains, fresh fruit from the market, or a strict lights-out rule after work? Share your best habit and let's swap ideas. #mindanaovas #nightshifthealth","body":{}},
{"id":"d11-laughs","day":11,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"Your brain at 4am, halfway through a client report","text":"“Remember that awkward thing you said in 2014? Let's replay it in full HD. Also, we're starving. Fried chicken. Right now. Then a nap. Then panic about the deadline.” What does your brain say at 4am? 👇"}},
{"id":"d12-am","day":12,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Let's build the Circle's night-shift playlist 🎧✨ Music can make 3am feel a lot less lonely. What's the one song that wakes you up, calms you down, or carries you through the final hour of your shift? Drop the song title below (no links, please) and find your next favourite in someone else's pick. #nightshiftplaylist #circlevibes","body":{}},
{"id":"d12-noon","day":12,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Set up quiet hours on both phones (yes, the work one too 📱). Most phones let you allow calls from chosen contacts only, so true emergencies still reach you while routine pings wait until you're awake. Then agree with each client on what counts as urgent and how to flag it. Not sure how to start that conversation? Circle Mentors is a good place to ask for a friendly script. Do you have quiet hours set up? How did your client react? #boundaries #vatips","body":{}},
{"id":"d12-hub","day":12,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Jeepneys, construction, karaoke next door 🏙️ Manila VAs, how do you sleep through the city's daytime noise after a night shift? Earplugs, a white-noise fan, a room at the back of the house, or simply being too tired to notice? Share your best tip below. #manilavas #daytimesleep","body":{}},
{"id":"d12-laughs","day":12,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: You set an hourly stretch reminder to look after your back. By 4am you've snoozed it six times, each time promising “right after this email,” and the only stretch so far was reaching for your coffee. Which reminder do you snooze the most? 👇"}},
{"id":"d13-am","day":13,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Sunrise check-in 🌅 Night-shift life can feel a little lonely when the rest of the world is just waking up. Who do you talk to after your shift? A housemate, a pet, a Circle BFF, or nobody yet? If you'd like some company, say hi below and connect with someone who keeps the same hours as you. And if the loneliness feels heavy, the Vent Room and Circle Wellness are here too. #nightshiftvas #circlebff","body":{}},
{"id":"d13-noon","day":13,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Treat your workspace like part of your toolkit. Screen at eye level, feet flat on the floor, elbows at roughly 90 degrees, and a reminder every hour to stand, stretch and look at something far away for 20 seconds. Small adjustments add up over long night shifts. If you have ongoing pain or discomfort, please check with Circle Wellness or a health professional. What's one change you've made to your setup? Share it below. #ergonomics #wfh","body":{}},
{"id":"d13-hub","day":13,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Cebu after dark 🌊 For VAs working nights in the city, what's your favourite way to recharge on a day off? Island hopping, a sunrise swim, a long nap, or a slow seaside breakfast? Share your ultimate reset day below! #cebuvas #restday","body":{}},
{"id":"d13-laughs","day":13,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"Night-shift VA starter pack","items":["Blackout curtains held up with tape and determination","Coffee number four, “just to stay focused”","A family group chat that's 200 messages ahead when you wake up","Saying “good morning” at 9pm with full confidence","A power bank charged like your life depends on it","An eye mask, earplugs and a household that still knocks","A sleep schedule best described as “flexible”","What's missing? Tell us below 👇"]}},
{"id":"d14-am","day":14,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Two weeks in, and look at you go! 🎉 Let's celebrate what you've learned about surviving the night shift. Maybe you found a sleep routine that works, discovered a healthier snack, or simply asked for help when you needed it. Share one thing you're proud of, and lift up someone else's win today. ✨ #vawins #nightshiftvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d14-noon","day":14,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Plan your rest days as seriously as your work days. Before the week starts, block them on your calendar and decide what they're for: catching up on sleep, errands, time with the people you love. Some night-shift VAs keep a similar sleep window on days off so the first shift back feels less like jet lag; others prefer a full reset. See what suits your body, and ask Circle Wellness if you're unsure. How do you spend your rest days? #worklifebalance #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d14-hub","day":14,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Davao heat check ☀️ Sleeping during the day is tough when the afternoon gets hot. Davao VAs, how do you keep your room cool enough to rest after a night shift? A fan pointed just right, a cool shower before bed, light curtains, or a nap schedule built around the heat? Share what works for you! #davaovas #restwell","body":{}},
{"id":"d14-laughs","day":14,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"Sunday evening, a VA on UK hours decides this is the week they finally eat well. Five neat containers of chicken, rice and vegetables go into the fridge, labelled Monday to Friday. Monday at 2am: eaten on schedule, and they feel unstoppable. Tuesday: still on track. Wednesday: a “quick task” turns into a two-hour fire drill, and dinner becomes a bag of chips eaten over the keyboard. Thursday: the containers stare at them every time the fridge opens. Friday: they eat two meals at once and call it “catching up.” What's your meal-prep win or disaster? Tell us below 👇"}},
{"id":"d15-am","day":15,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Every VA started somewhere 🌙 This week we're talking about finding first clients and writing proposals. Let's begin with your story: how did you land your very first client, or where are you in that search right now? If you're still looking, tell us what's been hardest so far, and the Circle can share ideas. Circle Jobs and Circle Mentors are good places to start, too. #firstclient #newvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d15-prompt","day":15,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"My first-ever job proposal was so bad that…","body":{}},
{"id":"d15-noon","day":15,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"The first two lines of your proposal matter most, because that's often all a busy client reads before deciding. Skip “Dear Sir/Madam, I am a hardworking VA…” and open with their problem: “You mentioned your inbox is overflowing and follow-ups are slipping. Here's how I'd fix that in week one.” Add one relevant example and a clear next step, and you're done. Try rewriting your opening line in the comments, and let's polish them together! #proposals #freelancetips","body":{}},
{"id":"d15-hub","day":15,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Cool, misty evening in the City of Pines? 🌲 Sounds like perfect proposal-writing weather. Baguio VAs, how are you finding your first (or next) clients: referrals, local businesses, online job boards, or Circle Jobs? Share what's worked for you, plus one tip for someone just starting out. #baguiovas #firstclient","body":{}},
{"id":"d15-laughs","day":15,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":97,"timer":"02:41:09","caption":"TrackerBot 3000, which you installed to “stay productive” while job hunting, catches you typing and deleting “I am a hardworking and passionate VA” for the ninth time.","punchline":"Words that survived: “Dear.” Activity: 97%. Progress: 0%. Rate your proposal-writing struggle from 1 to 10 in the comments."}},
{"id":"d16-am","day":16,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Sent a proposal this week? That counts. ✨ Whether it got a reply, a polite no or total silence, hitting send takes courage, and every proposal teaches you something for the next one. This week we're celebrating the brave clicks: first proposals, first discovery calls, first yeses. Drop your proposal count for the month in the comments. Zero is welcome too. This is a starting line, not a scoreboard. #firstclient #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d16-noon","day":16,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Using a proposal template? Smart, as long as it's a skeleton and not a copy-paste. Keep the structure, then rewrite three parts every time: the opening (their problem, in words from their post), the example (one that fits this exact job) and the closing question. Before you hit send, check the client's name, the job title and any instruction tucked into the post, like a keyword they asked you to include. Want a second pair of eyes on your template? Circle Mentors can be a great sounding board. Which line of yours never changes? #proposals #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d16-hub","day":16,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Before the night shift kicks off, a lounge question: when do you do your client hunting? 🌙 Some night-shift VAs write proposals right after waking up, others save them for a quiet hour around 2am. Which time works best for you, and why? #nightshift #proposals","body":{}},
{"id":"d16-laughs","day":16,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Client","text":"To prove you read the whole job post, start your proposal with the word 'mango'."},{"who":"Me","text":"Mango. I'd love to help organize your inbox. Here's a sample workflow I built just for this role."},{"who":"Client","text":"Out of 200 proposals, you're the only one who wrote mango!"},{"who":"Me","text":"So... I'm hired?"},{"who":"Client","text":"Shortlisted! Round two: same proposal, but as a haiku."}]}},
{"id":"d17-am","day":17,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Good morning to everyone just logging off. 🌙 Let's talk about the quiet part of client hunting: sending proposals and hearing nothing back. It can sting, especially after a long night. Silence usually says more about a crowded inbox than about your worth. How do you reset after a batch of no-replies? A walk, a nap, a fresh template? Share what helps. Someone reading this may need it today. #firstclient #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d17-noon","day":17,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"New to client hunting? Scammers know it, and they often target first-timers. Watch for these patterns: a 'hiring manager' who wants to move the chat to an outside messaging app within minutes; a 'training kit' or 'software fee' you must pay before starting; pay offered only in crypto; requests for your ID and a selfie before any contract exists. A real client pays you, never the other way around. Seen a suspicious post? Report it through Circle Scam-Buster, and tell us below which red flag you spot most often. #scamaware #vasafety","body":{}},
{"id":"d17-hub","day":17,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Luzon VAs, from Ilocos to Bicol 🌾 here's a client-hunting puzzle: which job-post phrase is hardest to decode? “Fast-paced environment,” “wear many hats,” “competitive pay”? Share the phrase that confuses you most, and if you've cracked one, tell us what it usually means in practice. Let's build a little job-post dictionary together. #luzonvas #firstclient","body":{}},
{"id":"d17-laughs","day":17,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"Write one perfect proposal, hit send, and wake up to three clients politely fighting over who gets to hire you.","reality":"Sent 38 proposals. Woke up to one automated “Thanks for applying!” Read it four times anyway, looking for hidden signs of interest. What's the most hope you've ever squeezed out of an auto-reply? 👇"}},
{"id":"d18-am","day":18,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"✨ Win check! Did you land a discovery call, a trial task or your very first client recently? Big or small, we want to cheer for it. Tell us in the comments what happened and, if you'd like, one thing in your proposal you think made the difference. Your 'what worked' might be exactly the hint someone else needs this week. #vawins #firstclient","body":{}},
{"id":"d18-noon","day":18,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"No client history yet? You still have proof, it's just wearing different clothes. Look back at past jobs, school projects, volunteering or helping with a family business, and translate them into VA terms: “handled bookings for a busy clinic front desk” shows scheduling and customer care. Pick the two examples that best match the job post and mention one early in your proposal. A Circle Academy certificate, like VA Foundations: Client Communication, can back you up too. What past experience could you turn into VA proof? #proposals #newvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d18-hub","day":18,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Island-hopping question for Visayas VAs 🏝️ If finding your first client were a trip between islands, which part was the longest boat ride: building your profile, writing proposals or waiting for replies? Share your answer, plus one tip for those still on the ferry. #visayasvas #firstclient","body":{}},
{"id":"d18-laughs","day":18,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"A VA at 2am, writing proposal #30","text":"'Dear Hiring Manager, I have always been deeply passionate about your inbox. Ever since I was a child, I have dreamed of organizing your calendar.'"}},
{"id":"d19-am","day":19,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Quick heart check this morning. 🌙 It's easy to scroll past a job post thinking 'I'm not ready yet', even when you match most of the requirements. Job posts are often wish lists, not strict checklists. Is there a post you almost skipped this week? Tell us about it in the comments and let's talk it through together. If the doubt feels heavier than usual, Circle BFF, the Vent Room and Circle Wellness are always open. #impostersyndrome #firstclient","body":{}},
{"id":"d19-noon","day":19,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Let's talk follow-ups. If a client viewed your proposal but went quiet, one polite nudge after 3–5 days is fair. Keep it short: thank them, add one new piece of value (a quick idea for their task), and ask a simple yes-or-no question, like 'Would a 15-minute call this week help you decide?' One follow-up is professional; five is pressure. How do you usually word yours? Share a version below (no client names) and let's polish them together. #followup #proposals","body":{}},
{"id":"d19-hub","day":19,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Climbing a mountain one step at a time: that's what landing a first client can feel like. 🌄 Mindanao VAs, what was your base-camp moment, the first small win that showed you could reach the top? A reply, a trial task, a kind no? Share it below for the climbers just starting out. #mindanaovas #firstclient","body":{}},
{"id":"d19-laughs","day":19,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: You spend 45 minutes tailoring the perfect proposal, read it three times, hit send with pride, and then notice it opens with 'Dear [Client Name],'."}},
{"id":"d20-am","day":20,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Shout-out to the kind “no” 💛 Not every reply is a yes, but some no's come with real kindness: a client who explained why, shared a quick note on your proposal, or said “please apply again next time.” Those replies help you grow, and they deserve a thank-you too. Have you received a no that actually helped? Share what it taught you in the comments (no client names), and cheer on someone who's still sending proposals. ✨ #gratitude #firstclient","body":{}},
{"id":"d20-noon","day":20,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Pricing your first proposals? Try this: research the typical range for the exact task (not just 'VA work'), pick a starting rate you can say out loud without apologizing, and attach a clear scope to it, such as 'up to 10 hours a week of inbox and calendar support'. Avoid 'I'll do anything for any rate'. It sounds eager but signals no boundaries. Circle Mentors can help you sanity-check your numbers. How did you choose your starting rate? #varates #proposals","body":{}},
{"id":"d20-hub","day":20,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Working from home means no more jeepney rides to the office, but face-to-face connections still count. 🚌 Manila VAs, have you ever found a client through someone you met in person, like a former officemate, a cousin's boss or a café meetup? Or has it all been online? Share how your first lead found you. #manilavas #firstclient","body":{}},
{"id":"d20-laughs","day":20,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"VA applying for their first client","items":["47 browser tabs of job posts, all 'saved for later'","A proposal template named FINAL_final_v9","Refreshing the inbox like it owes them money","Rewriting the profile headline for the eleventh time today","Practicing 'My rate is...' to the bathroom mirror","A cover letter that says 'detail-oriented' four times","Celebrating a 'Thanks, we'll be in touch'","What's in your job-hunt starter pack? Add it below 👇"]}},
{"id":"d21-am","day":21,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"As this week of client hunting wraps up, let's pause for a moment. 🌙 Whether you sent one proposal or fifty, landed a call or are still waiting, you showed up for your future self. What's one thing you learned about yourself while job hunting this week? Patience, a new skill, a better routine? Share it in the comments. And rest well after your shift. #firstclient #selfcare","body":{}},
{"id":"d21-noon","day":21,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Got a discovery call coming up? Prep three things: 1) Two questions about their biggest time-drain, like 'Which task do you wish you never had to touch again?' 2) A 30-second intro focused on what you can take off their plate. 3) A next-step offer, such as a paid trial week. Confirm the call time in both time zones the day before, and test your mic and lighting 10 minutes early. Want feedback on your questions first? A Circle Mentor can help. What question do you always ask on a first call? #discoverycall #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d21-hub","day":21,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Somewhere between the beach weekends and the busy city streets, Cebu VAs are building careers. 🌊 Quick question: if you could give one tip to someone in Cebu sending their very first proposal tonight, what would it be? Keep it short, like a postcard from the shore. #cebuvas #proposals","body":{}},
{"id":"d21-laughs","day":21,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"A VA lands their first discovery call: “Tuesday, 9am.” They iron a shirt, test the mic twice, rehearse their 30-second intro six times and log in at 8:50am Manila time, glowing. Nobody joins. At 9:15 they send a polite “Just checking in!” The reply arrives an hour later: “See you tonight! 9am MY time 🙂” The VA spends the day re-ironing the shirt and re-rehearsing the intro. That night the call goes beautifully, and the VA's very first question is: “Which time zone should we use for meetings?” Ever been caught by a time-zone mix-up? Tell us below 👇"}},
{"id":"d22-am","day":22,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Small upgrades deserve confetti too. 🎉 Did you set up a template, a shortcut, a shared calendar or a checklist that saved you time this month? Even 10 minutes a day adds up to hours. Share your favorite workflow win in the comments, and if it's simple enough, explain it in one sentence so others can try it tonight. #workflow #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d22-prompt","day":22,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"If TrackerBot 3000 wrote a report on my day, the headline would be…","body":{}},
{"id":"d22-noon","day":22,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Your time tracker can be a helpful teammate instead of a source of stress. Three habits: label every entry with the client and task ('Inbox cleanup, weekly'), stop the timer the moment you switch tasks, and review your week every Friday to spot what takes longer than you quoted. That review is gold when you renegotiate scope or rates. What's your biggest time-tracking headache? Tell us below and let's solve a few together. #timetracking #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d22-hub","day":22,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Some tools are like durian: you either love them or walk away fast. 😄 Davao VAs, which tool took you a while to appreciate, and which one did you drop for good? Spreadsheets, project boards, calendar apps? Tell us your love-it-or-leave-it tool. #davaovas #vatools","body":{}},
{"id":"d22-laughs","day":22,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":4,"timer":"02:47:19","caption":"Screenshot caught: a blank spreadsheet, a cursor blinking in cell A1, and zero mouse movement for nine minutes.","punchline":"TrackerBot 3000 calls it 'idle'. You call it 'building the formula in your head'. You have agreed to disagree, and the tracker has already flagged it for the client."}},
{"id":"d23-am","day":23,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Morning, night owls. 🌙 Before you close the laptop, a small workflow confession: what's one task you still do the slow way, even though you suspect there's a faster one? Copy-pasting the same reply, renaming files one by one, rebuilding the same report every week? No judgment here! Name it below. Someone in the Circle may have a shortcut for you, and you might have one for them. Then rest well. #workflow #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d23-noon","day":23,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Write it once, use it forever: that's the magic of an SOP (standard operating procedure). Next time you do a repeat task, record the steps as you go: what to open, what to check, what 'done' looks like. Add screenshots if they help, with any client details blurred. Now you can hand the task off, pick it back up after a break, or show a client how organized you are. Want feedback on your first one? Share a client-free version in your Circle Hub or ask a Circle Mentor. Which task would you document first? #sops #workflow","body":{}},
{"id":"d23-hub","day":23,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Cool Baguio nights are perfect for focus, but cold fingers on a keyboard are real. 🧣 What's in your work-from-home setup up here? A trusty planner, a second monitor, a warm blanket, a big thermos of something hot? Share your desk essentials, tech and non-tech. #baguiovas #wfhsetup","body":{}},
{"id":"d23-laughs","day":23,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Client","text":"Our workflow is a mess. We use way too many tools."},{"who":"Me","text":"Agreed! Let's move everything into one project board."},{"who":"Client","text":"Love it. I'll also add a new chat app, a new calendar and a new notes app."},{"who":"Me","text":"...to simplify?"},{"who":"Client","text":"Exactly. Oh, and I'll still send urgent tasks as voice notes at 3am."}]}},
{"id":"d24-am","day":24,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Tiny trophies, big pride. 🏆 This week let's celebrate the unglamorous wins: your first clean timesheet, an inbox at zero, a template that finally works, a client who noticed how organized everything looks. Which one would earn a spot on your trophy shelf? Tell us about it in the comments. Extra cheers if it took you more than one try! #vawins #workflow","body":{}},
{"id":"d24-noon","day":24,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"One scam pattern loves new VAs: the 'install our software' request. A 'client' says you must use their special time tracker or download files they send. Sometimes it's harmful software; sometimes it's a remote-access tool that lets them control your device. Another version: they 'send' money for equipment, then ask you to forward part of it to a 'vendor'. Only use tools you can verify yourself, never install files from strangers, and never forward money. Spotted one? Report it to Circle Scam-Buster. Which red flag would you add? #scamaware #vasafety","body":{}},
{"id":"d24-hub","day":24,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Dark mode crew, assemble. 🌙 What small settings make the night shift easier for you? A warm screen filter, a gentle reminder to take breaks, do-not-disturb hours for daytime sleep? Share your favorite tweak so everyone in the lounge can try it tonight. #nightshift #vatools","body":{}},
{"id":"d24-laughs","day":24,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"Client: \"Everything you need is in the shared drive, just search for it.\" You type the file name, press enter, and there it is.","reality":"214 files called \"Untitled document\", three folders named \"Misc\", a \"Misc (2)\" inside one of them, and a spreadsheet titled \"IMPORTANT, READ FIRST\" that is completely empty."}},
{"id":"d25-am","day":25,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Too many tabs, too many tools, too many notifications? 🌙 Tool overwhelm is real, especially when every client uses a different system. You don't have to master everything at once. Pick one tool to understand well this week and let the rest be 'good enough' for now. Which tool feels the most confusing right now? Tell us in the comments. Fellow members and Circle Mentors may have just the tip you need. #vatools #overwhelm","body":{}},
{"id":"d25-noon","day":25,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Time zones get trickier twice a year. Many countries switch to daylight saving time, but the Philippines doesn't, so a 10am New York call lands at 10pm in Manila in July but 11pm in January. The US, UK, Europe and parts of Australia change on different dates. Write meeting times in both zones, let your calendar app convert, and double-check recurring calls the week clocks change. To practise, try the 'Scheduling across time zones' lesson in Executive Support Essentials, then the time-zone scheduling simulator in Circle Academy. Has a clock change ever caught you out? #timezones #workflow","body":{}},
{"id":"d25-hub","day":25,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Luzon VAs, quick tools challenge for tonight ⌨️ From the Cordilleras to Batangas, what's the one keyboard shortcut or small trick that saves you the most time each shift? Pasting without formatting, a quick screenshot key, a saved search, a text expander? Drop yours below so the whole hub can try it before the week ends. #luzonvas #vatools","body":{}},
{"id":"d25-laughs","day":25,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"Your laptop, five minutes before a client call","text":"\"Installing update 1 of 37. Please don't turn off your device.\" *four minutes later* \"Almost there!\" *one minute later* \"Restarting to finish up.\" *call starts* \"Welcome! Let's set up a few things before you begin.\""}},
{"id":"d26-am","day":26,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Learned a new tool recently? That's a milestone worth celebrating! ✨ Maybe you wrote your first spreadsheet formula, designed a graphic in Canva, or set up a client's task board in Trello without a tutorial. Tell us what you learned and how long it took to click. Curiosity like that is what keeps a VA career growing. #newskills #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d26-noon","day":26,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Typing the same replies over and over? Build a small library of saved replies: a meeting confirmation, a 'received, working on it' note, a weekly update opener, a polite 'that's outside our current scope'. Store them in a doc or your email's template feature, and personalize the first line each time so they never feel robotic. A handful of good templates can save a lot of typing. Which message do you type most often? Share your favorite saved reply below (no client details). #templates #productivity","body":{}},
{"id":"d26-hub","day":26,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Working from a beach town or a small island? 🌊 Signal can come and go like the tide. What tools help you stay reliable when the connection drops: offline docs, scheduled emails, a pocket Wi-Fi, a backup spot in town? Share your island-proof setup with the Visayas crew. #visayasvas #remotework","body":{}},
{"id":"d26-laughs","day":26,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: The client's new 'all-in-one' system needs four logins, two verification codes, a password that expires every 30 days and a 45-minute onboarding video before you can answer one email."}},
{"id":"d27-am","day":27,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Stuck on a tool at 3am while your client is fast asleep? 🌙 Night shift can make small tech hiccups feel lonely, because there's nobody awake to ask. What's your plan when something won't work: search the help pages, check your SOP, switch to another task and leave a clear note for the morning, or ask in the Night Shift Lounge? Share your 'stuck at 3am' routine below. Someone working tonight might need it. #nightshift #vatools","body":{}},
{"id":"d27-noon","day":27,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"A simple board can calm a busy week. Try four columns: To Do, Doing, Waiting on Client, Done. That third column is the secret: it shows exactly where things are stuck, so your updates almost write themselves ('Three tasks are waiting on your approval'). It works in Trello, a spreadsheet or sticky notes on a wall. What columns does your board use? Share your setup in the comments so others can borrow ideas. #taskmanagement #workflow","body":{}},
{"id":"d27-hub","day":27,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Up in the hills or down in the city, here's a fun one for Mindanao VAs: paper planner or fully digital? 📒 Some VAs love writing tasks by hand before moving them into an app. Others haven't touched a pen in years. Which team are you on, and why? #mindanaovas #vatools","body":{}},
{"id":"d27-laughs","day":27,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"VA whose time tracker is always running","items":["Feels judged by the activity bar during every long email","Times snack breaks like a world-record attempt","Says 'One sec, let me stop my timer' to the whole family","Knows the exact second the next screenshot hits","Jumps at every camera-shutter sound, even on TV","Logs '0:02 - Thinking' with zero shame"]}},
{"id":"d28-am","day":28,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"That's a wrap on Tools & Workflows week! 🎉 Today let's celebrate wins by subtraction. Sometimes the best upgrade is something you stopped doing: an app you finally deleted, a notification you switched off, a meeting replaced by a written update, a step you cut from a checklist. What did you let go of this month, and how much calmer does your shift feel? Share it in the comments and inspire someone else to declutter too. #workflow #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d28-noon","day":28,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Handling client logins? Treat them like house keys. Ask clients to give you your own user account or delegated access instead of sharing their main password. Store credentials in a password manager, not in chat messages or a spreadsheet. Turn on two-step verification wherever you can, and keep a simple access list so offboarding is clean when a project ends. Clients notice this kind of care. How do you keep client access organized? Share your system below. #datasecurity #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d28-hub","day":28,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"City sounds are part of the Manila soundtrack: tricycles, a neighbor's karaoke night, a rooster with no sense of time. 🎧 What helps you focus and sound clear on calls through it all? Noise-canceling headphones, a mic filter, a quiet corner, a focus playlist? Share your best noise-beating tool. #manilavas #wfhsetup","body":{}},
{"id":"d28-laughs","day":28,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"It's Monday, and a VA decides this is the week they finally get organized. New project board. New notes app. New calendar colors: blue for meetings, green for deep work, orange for 'quick tasks'. By Wednesday the calendar is almost entirely orange. By Thursday they add a new color, red, for 'quick tasks that were not quick'. By Friday the whole week is red, and the VA calmly renames red to 'normal'. Next week's plan: a spreadsheet to track all the tools they use to track things. What's the most over-engineered system you've ever built?"}},
{"id":"d29-am","day":29,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Waking up to a client message that just says 'Can we talk?' can make anyone's stomach flip. 🌙 Often it turns out to be a schedule change or a new task, not a disaster. Still, those moments take courage. How do you calm your nerves before a hard conversation with a client? Deep breaths, notes ready, a quick chat with a friend? Share your ritual. And if you'd like someone to talk it through with first, Circle BFF is here. #clientcommunication #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d29-prompt","day":29,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"When a client says \"Can we hop on a quick call?\", what it actually means is…","body":{}},
{"id":"d29-noon","day":29,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Clear updates can prevent a lot of client worry. Try a 3-line update at the end of each shift: Done (what you finished), Doing (what's in progress and when it will be ready), Need (anything blocking you, like approvals or logins). It takes two minutes and answers 'How's it going?' before anyone asks. Night-shift VAs: schedule it to land at the start of your client's morning. What do you include in your updates? Share your format below. #clientupdates #communication","body":{}},
{"id":"d29-hub","day":29,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Cebu crew, the Queen City of the South knows how to keep its cool through busy seasons. 👑 When you need to share hard news with a client, like a missed deadline or a rate increase, do you prefer a call, a recorded video message or writing it out? Share what keeps you calm and clear. #cebuvas #clientcommunication","body":{}},
{"id":"d29-laughs","day":29,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":100,"timer":"00:47:12","caption":"Screenshot caught: a six-paragraph email to the client, deleted, rewritten twice, softened three times, then replaced with 'Sounds good!'","punchline":"47 minutes at 100% activity. Final output: two words and an exclamation mark. TrackerBot 3000 has never been prouder, or more confused."}},
{"id":"d30-am","day":30,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Brave conversation award goes to… you? 🏅 Did you ask for a rate increase, push back on scope creep, admit a mistake early or ask a client for feedback this month? Those talks are hard, and having them is a real milestone. Share your brave moment in the comments (no client names needed), and let's give each other a round of applause. #vawins #clientcommunication","body":{}},
{"id":"d30-noon","day":30,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"When a client asks for 'just one more thing' outside your agreement, try 'yes, and' instead of a flat no: 'Happy to help with that! It's outside our current scope, so it would add about 3 hours a week. Would you like me to add it at my usual rate, or swap it for another task?' You stay helpful, the client gets a clear choice, and scope creep gets a name. How do you usually handle extra requests? Share your go-to wording in the comments. #scopecreep #communication","body":{}},
{"id":"d30-hub","day":30,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Feedback can feel like peeling a pomelo: a little effort first, then the good part. 🍊 Davao VAs, how do you ask a client for feedback without it feeling awkward? A monthly check-in, a short form, a simple 'What should I keep doing?' Share the question that gets you the most useful answers. #davaovas #clientfeedback","body":{}},
{"id":"d30-laughs","day":30,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Client","text":"I have some feedback on the report. It needs more... pop."},{"who":"Me","text":"More pop, got it! Brighter colors, more charts, or a shorter summary?"},{"who":"Client","text":"Yes."},{"who":"Me","text":"...Which one?"},{"who":"Client","text":"Surprise me. But keep it exactly the same."}]}},
{"id":"d31-am","day":31,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Good morning, night owls 🌙 If you've just logged off, take a slow breath before anything else. We're a few days into client communication week, so here's a gentle one before you sleep: what's one message you find hardest to send a client? Asking for clarity, saying no, flagging a mistake? Share yours in the comments. You're probably not the only one, and naming it is often the first step to making it easier. #clientcomms #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d31-noon","day":31,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Scam-Buster check 🔎 Some red flags sound like ordinary client requests. Watch for: \"Can you open an e-wallet or bank account in your name for the business?\", \"Please receive a few packages at home and reship them\", or \"I'll send verification codes to your phone, just pass them to me.\" Requests like these can turn your identity into someone else's tool, and you may be the one left dealing with the fallout. A genuine client sets up their own accounts. If one lands in your inbox, pause and report it to Circle Scam-Buster. Which request would make you stop and check? #scamaware #staysafe","body":{}},
{"id":"d31-hub","day":31,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Cool Baguio evenings are made for honest chats 🌲 When a client's feedback stings a little, what helps you reset before replying? A walk in the fog, a warm blanket, a cup of something hot, a quick stretch? Tell us how you handle it, Baguio style. #baguio #clientfeedback","body":{}},
{"id":"d31-laughs","day":31,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"Client: \"Let's meet at 9 tomorrow!\" You set two alarms, prep your notes and join the call right on time.","reality":"You join at 9 your time. The client joins at 9 their time. In between: two calendar invites, three \"Are you on?\" messages and one very confused \"Wait, is it still today for you?\""}},
{"id":"d32-am","day":32,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Wins time ✨ Today we're celebrating the saves: a mix-up you caught before it grew, a confusing brief you turned into a clear plan, a tense thread that ended with \"Thanks, that's perfect!\" Good communication often looks like nothing went wrong, so these wins are easy to miss. Tell us about your recent save in the comments (no client names needed), big or tiny, and let's cheer each other on! 🎉 #vawins #clientcomms","body":{}},
{"id":"d32-noon","day":32,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Vague instructions like \"make it pop\" or \"just clean this up\" turn work into a guessing game, so don't guess. Reply with two or three concrete options and a default: \"Happy to! Do you mean brighter colours, fewer words or more charts? If I don't hear back by 3pm your time, I'll go with fewer words.\" Options are easier to answer than open questions, and the default keeps work moving while your client is busy. Save the format as a template for next time. How do you handle a fuzzy brief? Share your favourite clarifying question below. #vaskills #clientcomms","body":{}},
{"id":"d32-hub","day":32,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Shifts are starting in the Night Shift Lounge 🌙 A quick one before your first task: do you prefer sending client updates as a written message, a voice note or a short screen recording? Which feels least awkward at 2am? Tell us your style and why it works for you. #nightshift #clientupdates","body":{}},
{"id":"d32-laughs","day":32,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"The client after approving the first draft","text":"\"Love it! Just a few small tweaks 😊\" *attaches a 14-page document called small_tweaks_v3_FINAL_final2*"}},
{"id":"d33-am","day":33,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Let's talk about the word \"no\". Saying it to a client can feel huge, especially when you care about the job and the relationship. How do you turn down extra work or an unrealistic deadline while staying kind and professional? A go-to phrase, a template, a deep breath first? Share what works for you. And if this topic feels heavy right now, Circle BFF and the Vent Room are always open. 🌙 #boundaries #clientcomms","body":{}},
{"id":"d33-noon","day":33,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Feedback feels easier when you ask for it first. Try a short weekly check-in question: \"What's one thing that's working well, and one thing you'd like me to do differently?\" Write down what you hear, repeat it back in your own words, and confirm the next step. It turns feedback into a routine instead of a surprise. Want to practise staying calm when feedback is tough? Try the 'Calming an upset client' lesson in VA Foundations: Client Communication. Do you ask clients for feedback, or wait for it to arrive? #vaskills #feedback","body":{}},
{"id":"d33-hub","day":33,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Real talk for Luzon VAs 🚗 Between traffic, power outages and rainy-season Wi-Fi wobbles, calls don't always go to plan. When your connection drops in the middle of an important client call, what's your go-to backup message? Share your best wording so others can borrow it. #luzon #clientcalls","body":{}},
{"id":"d33-laughs","day":33,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: You send the client a tidy email with four numbered questions. They answer question 1. You resend questions 2 to 4, politely in bold. They answer question 1 again, with extra enthusiasm."}},
{"id":"d34-am","day":34,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Shout-out o'clock ✨ Let's spread some appreciation. Think of a client, teammate or fellow VA who communicates really well. What do they do that makes your work easier? Clear briefs? Fast replies? A simple \"thank you\" at the end of the week? Share it below (no names needed) so we can all learn from the good ones. 💛 #gratitude #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d34-noon","day":34,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Made a mistake on a client task? How you report it can matter as much as the mistake itself. Try this structure: 1) what happened, in one sentence; 2) what you've already done to fix it; 3) what you'll change so it doesn't happen again. Keep the apology short and lead with the solution. Not sure about your wording? Circle Mentors can help you look over a draft before you send it. What's your approach when something goes wrong? #vaskills #clientcomms","body":{}},
{"id":"d34-hub","day":34,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Island-hopping question 🏝️ Visayas VAs, with clients spread across so many time zones, how do you let them know when you're offline? A status message, an email signature, an auto-reply, a shared calendar? Share your setup, from Bohol to Iloilo to Leyte. #visayas #boundaries","body":{}},
{"id":"d34-laughs","day":34,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"Sending a client update starter pack","items":["Five drafts of a two-line message","\"Just circling back!\" (third circle today)","\"Per my last message\" typed, deleted, retyped nicer","\"Hope you're well!\" sent at 3am while barely well yourself","A screenshot attached, just in case","Reading their \"ok.\" with a full stop and spiraling for an hour","Replying \"Noted!\" to something you will think about forever"]}},
{"id":"d35-am","day":35,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"A gentle one as this week's theme wraps up 🌙 Think about a client conversation that felt hard recently. If you could replay it, what would you keep, and what would you change? There's no wrong answer, and learning out loud helps everyone. Share in the comments if you'd like. If a work conversation is still weighing on you, the Vent Room and Circle BFF are always here. #clientcomms #reflection","body":{}},
{"id":"d35-noon","day":35,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"An upset client message can make your heart race, but a calm structure helps. Try: 1) Acknowledge the feeling (\"I can see this is frustrating\"). 2) Own your part without over-apologising. 3) Give a clear next step and a time (\"I'll have the fix ready by 2pm your time\"). Then follow up exactly when you said you would. For a deeper walkthrough, see the 'Calming an upset client' lesson in VA Foundations: Client Communication, and practise with Circle Bestie's 'The 3AM angry client' scenario. What helps you stay calm? Share below. #clientcomms #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d35-hub","day":35,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"A Mount Apo-sized question for Mindanao VAs 🌄 If you could tell every new client one thing before day one, what would it be? Your working hours, how you like to receive feedback, the best way to reach you? Share your \"before we begin\" tip below. #mindanao #clientcomms","body":{}},
{"id":"d35-laughs","day":35,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"A VA spends forty minutes writing the perfect weekly update. Bullet points. Bold headings. A cheerful emoji, deleted, then added back. Every task, every link, every result, neatly organized. They hit send and feel like a true professional. Three days later, the client writes: \"Hey! Quick question, what have you been working on this week?\" The VA scrolls up. The update is still there. Unopened. Waiting patiently, like a message in a bottle. They copy it, paste it, and type \"Here you go! 😊\" with the calmest, most professional smile in history."}},
{"id":"d36-am","day":36,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"New week, new theme, and it's a money one 💸✨ We're talking rates, invoices and getting paid on time. To kick things off, let's celebrate: when did you last raise your rate, receive a payment early, or finally send that invoice you were nervous about? Share your money win, any size. Every step toward being paid fairly deserves a cheer! #vawins #getpaid","body":{}},
{"id":"d36-prompt","day":36,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"My invoice has been \"processing\" for so long that…","body":{}},
{"id":"d36-noon","day":36,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"A clear invoice is easier to pay than a confusing one. Include: your name and the client's, an invoice number, the dates covered, a short list of tasks or hours, the total, the due date and how to pay. Send it on the same day each cycle so clients learn your rhythm. A simple spreadsheet or template works fine. Want a second pair of eyes on yours? Ask in the comments or book a session with Circle Mentors. For tax questions, an accountant is the right person to ask. What's one thing you added to your invoices that made a difference? #invoicing #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d36-hub","day":36,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Between EDSA traffic and coffee-shop co-working, Manila VAs juggle a lot 🌆 If you work with more than one client, do you charge everyone the same rate, or does it depend on the work, the hours or the time zone? Share how you decide. #manila #varates","body":{}},
{"id":"d36-laughs","day":36,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":4,"timer":"00:52:08","caption":"Cursor parked on the refresh button of the \"Payment pending\" page. Same tab. Same face. Fifty-two minutes.","punchline":"TrackerBot 3000 marked it as \"idle.\" Excuse me, refreshing a payment page 300 times is finance work AND cardio."}},
{"id":"d37-am","day":37,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Money talk, gently 🌙 Rates can feel like a heavy topic, especially at the end of a long night. How did you decide on your current rate? Research, a chat with Circle Mentors, trial and error, or a number that just felt safe? There's no right answer. Sharing how you got there might help a newer VA find their footing. #varates #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d37-noon","day":37,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Client says your rate is over their budget? Try adjusting the scope, not the price: \"I understand. Within that budget I can cover inbox and calendar for 10 hours a week, and we can add social media later.\" Your rate stays steady, the client gets a real choice, and you avoid a discount that's hard to undo. If you do offer a trial price, put its end date in writing. Want to practise the conversation first? Talk it through with Circle Mentors. Has a client ever asked you for a discount? How did you respond? #varates #negotiation","body":{}},
{"id":"d37-hub","day":37,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"From Cebu City to the beaches of Mactan 🌊 here's a money-rhythm question: do you invoice clients weekly, every two weeks or monthly? Which schedule keeps your budget calmer between paydays? Share what works for you. #cebu #invoicing","body":{}},
{"id":"d37-laughs","day":37,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Client","text":"Before we start, what's your rate?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Here it is! 😊"},{"who":"Client","text":"Oh wow. And if it's just a few quick tasks?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Same rate. Quick tasks are still tasks."},{"who":"Client","text":"What if they're REALLY quick?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Then it'll be a really quick invoice."}]}},
{"id":"d38-am","day":38,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Paid-on-time party! 🎉 Did an invoice clear without a single reminder? Did you send your first-ever invoice, or start a savings pot? Tell us in the comments. Getting paid on time is worth celebrating, and your wins remind newer VAs that it's possible. ✨ #getpaid #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d38-noon","day":38,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Payment tricks are this Scam-Buster tip's focus 🔎 Be careful with: a \"client\" who overpays and asks you to send back the difference, pay offered only in crypto or gift cards, a \"payment sent\" screenshot used to rush you into starting, or a fee to \"unlock\" your earnings. A genuine client never needs you to send money in order to get paid. If a payment feels strange, pause and report it to Circle Scam-Buster. Seen any of these? Share the pattern (no links or names) so others can spot it. #scamaware #getpaid","body":{}},
{"id":"d38-hub","day":38,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Waiting on a late invoice can feel like waiting for the ferry to Samal: you know it's coming, but the wait tests your patience. ⛴️ Davao VAs, how do you remind a client about an overdue payment without feeling awkward? Share your go-to wording so others in the hub can borrow it. #davao #getpaid","body":{}},
{"id":"d38-laughs","day":38,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"You send the invoice on the 1st. The client pays on the 2nd. You celebrate with a nice dinner like the CEO you are.","reality":"Day 8: \"Just a gentle reminder! 😊\" Day 15: \"Following up on this!\" Day 22: \"Hope all is well!\" Day 30, client: \"Oh, was that for me?\" You, eating instant noodles: \"No worries at all!\""}},
{"id":"d39-am","day":39,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Night-shift brains and money admin don't always mix 🌙 When do you do your invoicing: right after a shift, on a day off, or at a set time each week? What helps you remember? A calendar reminder, a sticky note, an accountability buddy? Share your routine. It might save someone's sleepy future self. #invoicing #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d39-noon","day":39,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Want fewer late payments? Agree on payment terms in writing before work begins: when invoices go out, when they're due, which payment methods you accept, and what happens if a payment is late (for example, work pauses after a set number of days). Settling this upfront makes reminders feel routine, not personal. For anything legal, check with a qualified professional. Which payment terms have helped you most? Share them below. #contracts #getpaid","body":{}},
{"id":"d39-hub","day":39,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Picture this: a foggy Baguio morning, strawberries from La Trinidad and a client payment that just landed 🍓 What's your small reward when you get paid? A favorite meal, a new plant, or straight into savings? Tell us how you celebrate in the City of Pines. #baguio #payday","body":{}},
{"id":"d39-laughs","day":39,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"My brain, the second a client payment lands","text":"\"We're rich! Let's buy a new chair, a plant, a fancy dinner and...\" *three bill reminders pop up* \"...okay. One small dessert. To share.\""}},
{"id":"d40-am","day":40,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Money admin wins deserve a spotlight too ✨ Maybe you finally built an income tracker, sorted a month of receipts into one folder, numbered your invoices properly, or wrote your payment terms down before a new project. None of it is flashy, but this groundwork makes every payday calmer. Share your money-admin win below, big or small, and let's cheer the quiet stuff together! 🥂 #milestones #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d40-noon","day":40,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Are \"quick tasks\" quietly eating your income? Try tracking everything for one week: every message, every five-minute fix, every call that ran over. Then compare it with what you billed. If there's a gap, consider a minimum block (like 15 or 30 minutes) for small requests, or a monthly package that covers them. Unsure how to price a package? Circle Mentors is a good place to ask. Have you ever tracked your \"invisible\" work? What surprised you? #varates #timetracking","body":{}},
{"id":"d40-hub","day":40,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Tonight's Lounge question 🌙 Overnight and weekend hours sometimes come with a higher rate, and sometimes they don't. Do you charge more for night shifts? If you do, how did you bring it up with your client? If not, would you want to? Talk it through with us. #nightshift #varates","body":{}},
{"id":"d40-laughs","day":40,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: You suggest a higher rate for overnight hours and the client replies, \"But it's daytime for me!\" as if that settles it. You read it at 3am, under a desk lamp, next to your fourth coffee."}},
{"id":"d41-am","day":41,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Can we be honest about money worries for a moment? 🌙 Waiting on a late payment can affect sleep, plans and mood, especially after a long night shift. What helps you stay steady while you wait? A small emergency fund, a simple budget, talking it out with someone? Share what works for you. If money stress feels heavy, the Vent Room, Circle BFF and Circle Wellness are here, and if it ever feels like too much, please reach out to a local crisis line. #moneystress #selfcare","body":{}},
{"id":"d41-noon","day":41,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Hourly or packages? Both can work. Hourly is simple and fair when tasks change a lot. Packages (a set monthly fee for a clearly defined scope) give you steadier income and reward you for getting faster. Whichever you choose, write down exactly what's included and what counts as extra, and review it every few months. Want a second opinion on your numbers? Circle Mentors offers 1:1 sessions with Proven VAs. Which one do you use, and why? Share your reasons below. #varates #pricing","body":{}},
{"id":"d41-hub","day":41,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Rainy days can mean outages and lost hours ☔ Luzon VAs, do you keep a \"rainy-day fund\" for the weeks when work or payments slow down? How do you build it: a set amount from each payment, or whatever is left over? Share your saving tricks, from Ilocos to Bicol. #luzon #savings","body":{}},
{"id":"d41-laughs","day":41,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"Money-admin day starter pack","items":["A budget spreadsheet named \"Budget v2 (real this time)\"","Receipts in a shoebox, a phone folder and three different chats","Converts every purchase into hours worked: \"That's 20 minutes of inbox\"","A savings goal called \"Emergency\" and another called \"Actual emergency\"","Opens the bank app with one eye closed","Color-codes every expense, then needs a nap"]}},
{"id":"d42-am","day":42,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Gratitude round! ✨ Money week is wrapping up, so tell us: who or what helped you get paid fairly? A Circle Mentor's advice, a reminder template, a client who always pays on time, or the 'Saying no to scope creep' lesson in Circle Academy? Share your thank-you below, and let's keep lifting each other toward fair pay. 💛 #gratitude #getpaid","body":{}},
{"id":"d42-noon","day":42,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Late invoice? Build a reminder ladder once and reuse it. For example: one day after the due date, a polite nudge with the invoice attached. A week later, a firmer note that restates your agreed terms. After that, pause work until payment arrives, if your contract allows it. Keep every message short, calm and factual, and save the templates so you never have to write them tired. What's your reminder style? Share your wording below. #invoicing #getpaid","body":{}},
{"id":"d42-hub","day":42,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"When a payment travels across oceans to reach the Visayas 🏝️ transfer fees and exchange rates can quietly nibble at it. How do you handle that: build fees into your rate, ask the client to cover them, or accept them as part of the job? Share your approach, island to island. #visayas #getpaid","body":{}},
{"id":"d42-laughs","day":42,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"After a week of research, a VA finally decides to raise their rate. They write the message, then rewrite it nine times. They practise saying the new number out loud to the mirror, then to the cat, then to the electric fan. They add \"I completely understand if this doesn't work for you\" and delete it. They hit send at 2am and lie awake planning a backup career in baking. At 8am, the client replies: \"Sounds fair! Thanks for letting me know.\" The VA stares at the screen for a full minute. Then opens a new draft titled: \"Should I have asked for more?\""}},
{"id":"d43-am","day":43,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Before you rest today, one safety question 🌙 Scam messages often show up when you're tired, late at night or worried about money. What's one rule you always follow before replying to a job offer from someone you don't know? Share yours. It might protect someone in the Circle this week. #scamaware #staysafe","body":{}},
{"id":"d43-prompt","day":43,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"You know a \"job offer\" is a scam when the \"recruiter\" says…","body":{}},
{"id":"d43-noon","day":43,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Real clients leave a trail you can check. Before accepting a new role: look for a consistent company presence, ask for a video call with the person you'll actually work for, get the scope and rate in a written agreement, and never pay to start a job. If anything feels off, run it past Circle Scam-Buster before you reply. A real opportunity will still be there after you've checked. What's on your checklist? Share it below. #scamaware #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d43-hub","day":43,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"From Cagayan de Oro to Zamboanga, are you the go-to person in your family for anything online? 🌄 When a cousin, neighbor or friend forwards you a \"job offer\", how do you help them check it? A quick call, a list of red flags, a run through Circle Scam-Buster together? Share your approach (no personal details or links, please). #mindanao #scamaware","body":{}},
{"id":"d43-laughs","day":43,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":100,"timer":"00:00:07","caption":"A message preview reading \"Congrats, you're hired! Just pay a small $50 training fee 😊\" and the cursor already on \"Block & Report\".","punchline":"Seven seconds at 100% activity: the shortest task of the shift and the best time saved all week. Zero hours lost to a fake job."}},
{"id":"d44-am","day":44,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Scam dodgers, this one's for you ✨ Did you spot a fake job post, ignore a pushy \"recruiter\", or warn a friend before they paid a \"fee\"? That's a real win, and it deserves applause. Share your scam-spotting moment in the comments (leave out personal details and links) and help someone else stay safe. 🛡️ #scamaware #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d44-noon","day":44,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Your ID is valuable, so share it carefully. A legitimate client may need some details for a contract or payment, but usually only after an offer is agreed and through a clear, official process. Be cautious if someone asks for ID photos or a selfie holding your ID during a first chat. Banking logins, PINs and one-time codes are different: never share them with anyone, at any stage. If you do share an ID copy, watermark it with the date and purpose, like \"For contract with [client] only.\" Unsure? Check with Circle Scam-Buster. What's your rule for sharing documents? #datasafety #scamaware","body":{}},
{"id":"d44-hub","day":44,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Busy city, busy inboxes 🌆 Manila VAs, which scam patterns have been popping up lately? A fake \"HR department\", a \"too easy\" data entry job, an urgent \"verify your account\" message? Share the pattern (no links or names, please) so the hub can stay one step ahead. #manila #scamaware","body":{}},
{"id":"d44-laughs","day":44,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Recruiter","text":"Easy online job! Just like a few product videos and earn commission. Here's your first PHP 150 bonus!"},{"who":"Me","text":"Oh. It actually paid."},{"who":"Recruiter","text":"Great, right? Now unlock VIP tasks. Just top up PHP 5,000 for your bigger commission."},{"who":"Me","text":"So the job pays me... after I pay you?"},{"who":"Recruiter","text":"Exactly! Very simple."},{"who":"Me","text":"Very simple indeed. Screenshot, Circle Scam-Buster, block. Done in one minute 🔎"}]}},
{"id":"d45-am","day":45,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Sleepy eyes, sharp instincts 🌙 If you could go back to your very first week as a VA, which scam warning sign would you want someone to tell you about? Upfront fees, rushed hiring, pay that sounds unbelievably high? Share it below. Your answer could be exactly what a brand-new VA needs to read today. #scamaware #newvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d45-noon","day":45,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"One pattern worth knowing this week 🔎 Some scams start politely on a trusted platform, then push you to move to an outside chat app \"for faster communication.\" Once there, the pressure builds: urgent deadlines, requests for ID photos, bank details or a selfie, and sometimes an \"interview\" done entirely by text. Keep early conversations where verification and reporting exist. You can always say, \"I'm happy to continue here.\" Spotted this pattern? Report it to Circle Scam-Buster and share the warning signs below. #scamaware #staysafe","body":{}},
{"id":"d45-hub","day":45,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Sun's setting over the Cebu skyline 🌅 Safety question for the hub: some fake recruiters borrow the name of a real company to look legit. How do you check that a recruiter really works where they say? Official contact channels, a video call, the company's own careers page? Share your steps (no names or links, please) so newer Cebu VAs can learn from them. #cebu #scamaware","body":{}},
{"id":"d45-laughs","day":45,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"Scams will be easy to spot. All caps. Ten exclamation marks. \"CLICK HERE TO WIN!!!\"","reality":"A polite \"HR coordinator,\" a neat logo, a calendar invite, a contract that looks almost real, and one tiny line: \"refundable onboarding fee.\" That one line is the whole scam. Real jobs pay you, not the other way around."}},
{"id":"d46-am","day":46,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Security wins deserve confetti too! ✨ Turned on two-step verification for your email? Moved your passwords into a password manager? Finished Circle Verified so clients know you're really you? Small habits like these keep scammers out of your accounts. Share your latest account-safety win below, and tell us which one you'd recommend to a newer VA. 🎉 #scamawareness #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d46-noon","day":46,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Give any new \"company\" a 5-minute background check: 1) Search its name together with words like \"review\" or \"scam\". 2) Check that the recruiter's email matches the company's own website domain, not a free email account. 3) Compare the offer with the company's official careers page, because scammers often copy real job titles word for word. If the details don't line up, paste the offer into Circle Scam-Buster for an instant risk check. What's the first thing you look up about a new company? #scamawareness #vatips","body":{}},
{"id":"d46-hub","day":46,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Davao VAs, has a \"client\" ever claimed to be from your own city just to win your trust faster? 🌄 Scammers sometimes drop a local business name, a familiar school or a \"friend of a friend\" to lower your guard. How did you check whether they were real? Share your experience so our Davao neighbors can spot the trick. #davaovas #scamawareness","body":{}},
{"id":"d46-laughs","day":46,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"A total stranger, texting a \"wrong number\"","text":"\"Hi, is this the dentist? Oh, sorry, wrong number! 😊 But since we're chatting... would you like a part-time job? Just like a few videos and earn $200 a day! First, a small deposit to unlock your tasks 🎉\" (Who else gets these \"wrong number\" job offers? 👇)"}},
{"id":"d47-am","day":47,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Morning, night owls 🌙 If you've just wrapped up a long shift, here's a gentle one before you sleep. Have you ever had an uneasy feeling about a job message, even when everything looked fine on paper? That gut feeling is worth listening to. What made you pause, and what did you do next? No judgment here. Sharing helps someone else trust their instincts too. Rest well after! #scamawareness #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d47-noon","day":47,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Know the \"task job\" trap. It starts small: you're paid a few dollars to like videos or rate products, and the first payouts really arrive. Then you're told to deposit money to unlock bigger tasks or to withdraw your earnings. The balance on screen keeps growing, but the real money never comes back. Real work never asks you to pay in so you can get paid out. The 6 red flags lesson in the Scam-Proof Freelancing course covers this pattern. Have you seen a task offer like this? #scamawareness #getpaid","body":{}},
{"id":"d47-hub","day":47,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"The Session Road crowd may be heading home, but scam messages don't keep office hours. 🌲 Tonight's question: has a \"client\" ever pushed you to move the chat to a private messaging app within minutes? What did you reply? Share your best line so fellow Baguio VAs can borrow it. #baguiovas #scamawareness","body":{}},
{"id":"d47-laughs","day":47,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: You ask the \"client\" for a quick video call and suddenly their camera is broken, their mic is broken, their laptop is broken, their internet is broken... but somehow the payment link for the $500 \"starter kit\" works perfectly. Seen this plot twist too? 👇"}},
{"id":"d48-am","day":48,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Gratitude corner ✨ If you've ever warned a friend about a fake job, or flagged a suspicious listing to Circle Scam-Buster, thank you. Looking out for each other is what makes a Circle a Circle. Who has helped you stay safe online? A friend, a mentor, a family member? Give them a shout-out below (roles or first names only, please) and tell us what they taught you. 💛 #scamawareness #gratitude","body":{}},
{"id":"d48-noon","day":48,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Your identity can be misused in one quiet way: account renting. A \"client\" asks you to open a bank or e-wallet account for \"payroll\", or to let them use yours to receive payments from their customers. This is a common way stolen money gets moved, and the account holder can end up facing the consequences. Never open accounts for an employer or lend yours out. The Protect your identity lesson in Scam-Proof Freelancing covers more ways to keep your details safe. Has anyone ever asked you to receive money for them? #scamawareness #idsafety","body":{}},
{"id":"d48-hub","day":48,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Scam messages can land at any hour, but the quiet hours are the tricky ones. 🌙 At 3am you're tired, and tired brains say yes too fast. What's your trick for staying sharp late at night? A rule like \"no big decisions before sleep\", or a friend you check with first? Share it with the lounge. #nightshift #scamawareness","body":{}},
{"id":"d48-laughs","day":48,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"Fake job offer starter pack","items":["\"Hiring URGENTLY!!! 🔥🔥🔥\"","$75/hour for simple copy-paste work","No interview, just \"trust the process\"","A small \"training kit\" fee before day one","\"Let's move this chat somewhere private\"","Asks for your ID before your name","Pays only in a crypto coin nobody has heard of","Spotted another red flag? Add it in the comments 👇"]}},
{"id":"d49-am","day":49,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Gentle one before you sleep 🌙 Getting caught by a scam doesn't mean you were careless. Scammers practise pressure and polish every single day. If it ever happened to you, what helped you recover? Reporting it, changing passwords, talking to someone you trust? Share only what you're comfortable with, so anyone carrying that shame feels less alone. And if it still weighs on you, Circle BFF, the Vent Room and Circle Wellness are here. #scamawareness #selfcare","body":{}},
{"id":"d49-noon","day":49,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Urgency is a scammer's favorite tool. \"Reply in 10 minutes.\" \"Only 2 slots left.\" \"Move to this other app now.\" Real clients usually give you time to think. Try a simple workflow: pause, screenshot the offer, paste it into Circle Scam-Buster for a risk check, then decide. Want to sharpen your eye? The Scam-Proof Freelancing course in Circle Academy walks through the 6 red flags, with a quick knowledge check at the end of each lesson. What's your go-to reply when someone tries to rush you? #scamawareness #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d49-hub","day":49,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Scam safety starts at home, Luzon VAs. 🌏 Relatives often get the same fake job texts and \"you've won a prize\" messages we do. How do you help the people you live with spot them? A family group chat rule, an \"ask me before you reply\" habit, a red flag you've taught your parents? Share what works, from Ilocos to Bicol. #luzonvas #scamawareness","body":{}},
{"id":"d49-laughs","day":49,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"A VA gets a message: \"Hi dear, you have been selected for a remote job paying up to $5,000 a week.\" She never applied. The job title is \"Virtual Assistant Manager Executive Specialist.\" The interview is a list of questions sent by text, including \"What is your bank PIN, for payroll setup?\" She asks for the company name. They send a logo, spelled two different ways. She asks where the office is. They reply, \"We are fully remote. Even the office.\" She reports it to Circle Scam-Buster, logs off, and goes back to her real client, who still can't find the file she sent yesterday. Ever met a \"recruiter\" like this? Share the red flags below. 👇"}},
{"id":"d50-am","day":50,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"New week, new theme: boundaries and rest! 🌿 And yes, rest is something to celebrate. Did you log off on time this week? Take a full day off? Say \"I'll handle that tomorrow\" without the guilt? Those are all wins. Share your smallest (or biggest) boundary win below, and let's cheer every single one. ✨ #boundaries #restisproductive","body":{}},
{"id":"d50-prompt","day":50,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"I set my status to \"Offline: back at 9am\" and the client replied…","body":{}},
{"id":"d50-noon","day":50,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Boundaries work best when they're written down. Add three lines to your client onboarding notes: your working hours (with time zone), your usual reply time, and how to reach you in a real emergency. Then block those hours in your calendar app. Clients aren't mind readers, and clear rules are kinder than quiet resentment. Not sure how to bring it up? Circle Mentors can help you word it kindly. What's your standard reply time? #boundaries #vatips","body":{}},
{"id":"d50-hub","day":50,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Island life has its own rhythm: slow tides, long sunsets. 🌊 Does your work rhythm match? Tonight's question for Visayas VAs: what's one boundary that helps you actually enjoy your off-hours? A beach day, a long family lunch, a phone-free hour? Share yours! #visayasvas #boundaries","body":{}},
{"id":"d50-laughs","day":50,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":62,"timer":"02:04:51","caption":"Captured on a Saturday: the VA's own out-of-office message open in one window, and a long reply to a client email being typed right underneath it.","punchline":"TrackerBot 3000: \"Logged: two hours of work on your day off.\" The VA: \"That doesn't count. I was in pajamas and lying down.\" Who else has broken their own out-of-office? 👇"}},
{"id":"d51-am","day":51,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Gentle check-in after your shift 🌙 When did you last take a real break, the kind with no notifications and no \"just checking one thing\"? If it's been a while, that's okay. Today could be the day. What does rest look like for you? A nap, a walk, a show, quiet time with family? Share it below. Someone might need the idea. And if you're running on empty, Circle Wellness is here for you. #rest #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d51-noon","day":51,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Try the \"Yes, and here's when\" reply. Instead of dropping everything for a new request, say: \"Happy to help! I can start this tomorrow at 10am, after I finish the report. Does that work, or should I move something?\" You stay helpful, your client sees your workload, and your hours stay protected. Want feedback on your wording? Share a draft in your Circle Hub. What's your favorite polite way to say \"not right now\"? #boundaries #clientcommunication","body":{}},
{"id":"d51-hub","day":51,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Mindanao has mountains worth climbing and views worth pausing for. 🌄 Rest is part of every climb, too. What's your go-to way to recharge after a heavy work week? A trip out of town, a big family meal, or just a long, guilt-free sleep? Tell us how Mindanao VAs reset! #mindanaovas #rest","body":{}},
{"id":"d51-laughs","day":51,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Client","text":"Hope you're enjoying your day off! 😊"},{"who":"Me","text":"I am, thank you!"},{"who":"Client","text":"Amazing. Totally unrelated, where's the March report saved?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Shared drive, in the folder called Reports."},{"who":"Client","text":"Perfect! And how do I open the shared drive?"},{"who":"Me (to the Circle)","text":"And that's how my day off became a training session. Who else has had a \"totally unrelated\" question eat their rest day? 👇"}]}},
{"id":"d52-am","day":52,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Raise your hand if you said \"no\" this week and the world kept spinning. 🙋✨ Saying no to extra unpaid work, a 2am call, or a task outside your scope is a milestone worth celebrating. Share your proudest \"no\" (or \"not yet\") in the comments. Bonus points if you said it kindly and clearly. Your boundaries make this whole Circle stronger. #boundaries #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d52-noon","day":52,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Strong boundaries are also a strong scam shield. 🔎 Many scams work by pushing past them: \"I need this done now.\" \"Don't tell anyone.\" \"Send the payment before you log off.\" If a request breaks your normal process, pause and verify it through a channel you already trust. A real client will understand a short delay. Tired and unsure? Wait until you've rested before deciding, and ask Circle Scam-Buster for a second look. What's your verify-first rule? #scamawareness #boundaries","body":{}},
{"id":"d52-hub","day":52,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Manila days fill up fast with traffic, errands and night shifts. 🚦 That makes your off-hours precious! How do you protect them? A \"no work chat after shift\" rule, a weekend that stays a weekend, or a cozy corner you escape to? Share your boundary tips, Manila VAs. #manilavas #boundaries","body":{}},
{"id":"d52-laughs","day":52,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"You write a calm, professional boundaries email. Your hours are clear. Your reply times are clear. You hit send and feel like a CEO.","reality":"You refresh your inbox every few minutes wondering if they're upset, then answer their 10pm message \"just this once\"... for the fourth night in a row. Anyone else? 👇"}},
{"id":"d53-am","day":53,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Let's talk gently about burnout today. 🌙 What's one sign that tells you you're getting close to it? For some, it's dreading every notification sound. For others, it's feeling tired even after sleep. Noticing early is a kind thing to do for yourself. Share your early warning sign if you're comfortable. And if things feel heavy right now, Circle BFF, the Vent Room and Circle Wellness are always open, and a local crisis line is there if you need urgent support. 💛 #burnout #selfcare","body":{}},
{"id":"d53-noon","day":53,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Build a 10-minute \"shutdown ritual\" that really ends your workday: 1) Jot loose thoughts into a \"parking lot\" note so they don't follow you to bed. 2) Send a short end-of-day update. 3) Log out of work chat on your phone, not just your laptop. 4) Do one physical \"off switch\", like changing clothes or stepping outside. For step 2, The 3-part status update lesson in VA Foundations: Client Communication gives you a simple Done, Next, Blockers format. What would you add to this list? #productivity #boundaries","body":{}},
{"id":"d53-hub","day":53,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Cebu VAs, honest answer time! 🌊 On a day off, does the work phone stay home, or does it come along to the beach \"just in case\"? If you've managed to leave it behind, what did you set up with your clients first? An auto-reply, a backup contact, a clear \"back on Monday\"? Share your rule for a real day off. #cebuvas #rest","body":{}},
{"id":"d53-laughs","day":53,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"The client at 4:59pm on a Friday","text":"\"Hey! Small favor before you log off 😊 Can you redo the whole Q3 presentation, make it 'pop', and have it ready by Monday 8am? Enjoy your weekend!!\" (What's the wildest 4:59pm request you've seen? 👇)"}},
{"id":"d54-am","day":54,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Milestone check! 🏅 Have you taken your first full week off since starting your VA career? Or finally stopped working through lunch? Rest milestones count just as much as income milestones. Tell us the rest win you're proudest of, and if you're still working toward one, tell us that too. We'll cheer you on either way. ✨ #restisproductive #milestones","body":{}},
{"id":"d54-noon","day":54,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Low rates often lead to long hours. If you need 60 hours a week just to cover your bills, burnout is waiting around the corner. Try this: add up your monthly costs, savings and a buffer for taxes, then divide by the billable hours you actually want to work in a month (admin time and unpaid days don't count). Treat that number as your minimum hourly rate, and plan small, steady increases with each new client or skill. Circle Mentors can help you sanity-check the numbers. What would change if you worked 10 fewer hours a week? #varates #burnout","body":{}},
{"id":"d54-hub","day":54,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Davao VAs, how do you plan a real day off? 🌄 Do you book it weeks ahead and tell your clients, or wait until you're already running on empty? Share how you schedule your rest, whether it's a Samal Island trip planned in advance or a lazy weekend you guard like a deadline. #davaovas #rest","body":{}},
{"id":"d54-laughs","day":54,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: First day off in months. Notifications off, auto-reply on, laptop hidden in a drawer. You're finally at the beach. A stranger nearby says \"quick question\" and your whole body replies \"Noted, will check and get back to you!\" Who else? 🙋"}},
{"id":"d55-am","day":55,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Gentle question after your shift 💛 What's one thing you stopped doing that gave you back some rest? Checking messages in bed, saying yes to every weekend task, scrolling until sunrise? Letting go of a habit can be just as restful as adding a new one. Share yours below. Your small change might be exactly what another tired VA needs to hear today. #selfcare #nightshift","body":{}},
{"id":"d55-noon","day":55,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Notification overload is a quiet cause of burnout. Try \"communication windows\": check messages at set times, say every 90 minutes, and tell your client when those times are. For true emergencies, agree on one channel only, like a phone call. Turn off non-urgent alerts the rest of the time. You'll do deeper work and feel less on edge. How often do you check messages now, and what would your ideal window be? #productivity #boundaries","body":{}},
{"id":"d55-hub","day":55,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Baguio VAs, after a long week, where does your rest happen? 🌲 A slow walk around Burnham Park, a stroll through the night market, a trip out to the strawberry farms, or a full day indoors with the pine view? Share your favorite way to unwind in the City of Pines so fellow Baguio VAs can borrow the idea. #baguiovas #rest","body":{}},
{"id":"d55-laughs","day":55,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"Overbooked VA starter pack","items":["Three clients, one brain, zero lunch breaks","Lunch eaten standing up, between two calls","Says \"I have a hard stop at 5\" and never stops","A calendar so full it needs its own calendar","Three chat apps open, all with red dots","\"I'll rest this weekend\" (every weekend)","Snoozes the \"log off now\" alarm like it's a suggestion","What's missing from this pack? Tell us below 👇"]}},
{"id":"d56-am","day":56,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Who covers for you so you can rest? 💛 Maybe it's a partner who handles dinner during your night shift, a sibling who keeps the house quiet while you sleep, or a fellow VA who backs you up when you're sick. Today, let's thank the people who make rest possible. Mention them by role (no names or handles needed) and tell us what they do for you. ✨ #gratitude #restisproductive","body":{}},
{"id":"d56-noon","day":56,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Scope creep is a sneaky source of burnout: one \"small extra\" at a time, until your role has doubled. Once a month, compare what you actually did (your time tracker helps) with the written list of tasks you were hired for. If the extras keep growing, bring both lists to your client and propose an updated scope or rate. The Saying no to scope creep lesson in VA Foundations: Client Communication covers the wording, and Circle Bestie's Unpaid extra work scenario lets you practise the conversation. Which \"small extra\" crept into your role? #scopecreep #boundaries","body":{}},
{"id":"d56-hub","day":56,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Lounge question for your nights off 🌙 Do you stay on night-owl hours, or flip back to daytime so you can see family and friends? How does your body feel when you switch back for the next shift? Share what works for you. Everyone's rhythm is different, and if sleep keeps slipping away, Circle Wellness is here. #nightshift #rest","body":{}},
{"id":"d56-laughs","day":56,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"Friday night, a VA finally plans a full weekend off. She writes the perfect out-of-office message. She tells her client twice. She hides the laptop under a pile of laundry. Saturday morning, her phone buzzes. Panic. It's... a promo text from a food delivery app. She laughs and goes back to sleep. Sunday, it buzzes again. This time it really is the client: \"Hope you're having a great weekend! No need to reply, see you Monday.\" She stares at it for a full minute, unsure if she's dreaming. Turns out boundaries actually work. Who knew? Has a boundary ever surprised you like this? Tell us below."}},
{"id":"d57-am","day":57,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Quiet question for your wind-down 🌙 This week we're talking about learning new skills. No pressure, just curiosity: if you had one free hour a week to learn something, what would you pick? A new tool, a design skill, better writing, a new language? Tell us below. Small steps add up, and resting first is always allowed. #upskilling #circleacademy","body":{}},
{"id":"d57-prompt","day":57,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"The client saw \"fast learner\" on my profile and asked me to master…","body":{}},
{"id":"d57-noon","day":57,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Picking what to learn next? Use the \"one client, one skill\" test. Look at job posts from your current or dream clients and list the tools and skills they mention most. Learn the one that keeps showing up. One focused skill you can prove beats five half-finished certificates. If inbox, calendar or data work keeps appearing, the free Executive Support Essentials course in Circle Academy has a practice simulator for each of the three. What skill keeps appearing in the job posts you like? #upskilling #circleacademy","body":{}},
{"id":"d57-hub","day":57,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Rainy afternoons in Luzon are made for staying in, and maybe for learning something new. 🌧️ Have you turned that indoor time into study time, with a quick Circle Academy module or a practice simulator? Share what you're learning lately and where you squeeze it in, Luzon VAs! #luzonvas #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d57-laughs","day":57,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":100,"timer":"00:04:38","caption":"Screenshot caught: a pivot table tutorial on the left, the client's spreadsheet on the right, and a pivot table that has somehow turned every name into a number.","punchline":"Client, 4 minutes ago: \"Can you do pivot tables?\" VA: \"Of course!\" VA now: speed-running an entire course while TrackerBot 3000 records 100% activity and 100% panic. What's your \"learn it in 5 minutes\" story? 👇"}},
{"id":"d58-am","day":58,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Certificate unlocked? 🎓✨ Whether you finished a full Circle Academy course, passed a simulator, or just learned one new shortcut this month, it counts! Learning while working is a big deal. Share your latest learning win below, big or tiny, and tell us what's next on your list. Let's turn this thread into a wall of wins! #upskilling #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d58-noon","day":58,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Courses teach, but projects prove. After each lesson, build one small sample using made-up data. Finished Inbox triage in 4 buckets? Sort a mock inbox and write a one-page triage plan. Done with Scheduling across time zones? Plan a pretend meeting week for clients in three time zones. Keep every sample in one portfolio folder, so when a client asks, \"Have you done this before?\", you can show, not just tell. Which lesson would you turn into a sample first? #portfolio #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d58-hub","day":58,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"From Iloilo to Bohol to Leyte, Visayas VAs are spread across so many islands, but learning connects us all. 🌊 What skill are you learning right now, and would you like a study buddy from another island? Drop your skill below and find your match! #visayasvas #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d58-laughs","day":58,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Client","text":"Do you know how to build automations?"},{"who":"Me","text":"I know the basics, and I learn fast!"},{"who":"Client","text":"Perfect! We need 12 of them, connected to 4 different apps."},{"who":"Client","text":"By tomorrow morning. Should be easy for you! 😊"},{"who":"Me (inner voice)","text":"Time to book a Circle Mentor. Possibly three."},{"who":"Me (to the Circle)","text":"Anyone free for an emergency study session tonight? 👇"}]}},
{"id":"d59-am","day":59,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Learning something new can feel scary, and that's completely normal. 🌙 Maybe you're worried about being \"too slow\" or \"not techy enough\". Whatever is holding you back, you're welcome here. What's one skill you've been nervous to start, and what's one tiny first step you could take this week? Share it below, and let's encourage each other kindly. #upskilling #youcandoit","body":{}},
{"id":"d59-noon","day":59,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Quick safety note for learning week. 🔎 Some scams pose as training programs: \"Pay for this certificate and we guarantee you a $2,000/month client.\" A real course can teach skills, but no course can promise a job. Red flags: guaranteed income, pressure to pay today, \"training fees\" that suddenly become a job requirement, and certificates nobody can verify. If an offer looks off, share it with Circle Scam-Buster before paying. Have you seen a \"guaranteed job\" course? #scamawareness #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d59-hub","day":59,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Mount Apo wasn't climbed in one step, and new skills aren't learned in one day either. 🌄 Mindanao VAs, what's a skill you picked up recently, and how has it helped your work? Bonus question: which skill should our hub learn together next? #mindanaovas #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d59-laughs","day":59,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"You'll finish this 6-week online course in 6 weeks. One module a week, color-coded notes, a calm and balanced learning journey.","reality":"Week 1: three modules, glowing. Weeks 2 to 5: \"I'll catch up this weekend.\" Week 6, 3am: four modules at 2x speed, a cold cup of coffee, whispering \"I've basically mastered it.\" Be honest: which week are you on? 👇"}},
{"id":"d60-am","day":60,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Asking for help is a learning win too! 🎓✨ Did you post a \"beginner\" question in your hub, book a session with a Circle Mentor, or ask a fellow VA to explain the formula that kept breaking? Brave questions are how skills grow. Share a time asking for help moved you forward this week, and cheer on anyone who's still working up the courage. #upskilling #celebratewins","body":{}},
{"id":"d60-noon","day":60,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Your new skills deserve a spotlight. Update your profile with the skill, add one work sample, and mention it in your next client check-in: \"I recently completed training in X. Happy to help with Y if it's useful.\" New skills are also a fair reason to review your rates with new clients. A session with a Circle Mentor who has been through a rate review can help you plan that conversation. Which new skill will you add to your profile this month? #upskilling #vacareer","body":{}},
{"id":"d60-hub","day":60,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Busy city, busy minds! 🏙️ Manila VAs, what are you learning these days? Spreadsheets, design, project management, a new language? Let's start a little study challenge: share your skill and your weekly study goal below, then check back next week to cheer each other on. #manilavas #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d60-laughs","day":60,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"The job post for an \"entry-level\" VA","text":"\"Requirements: 10 years of experience. Expert in 14 software tools. Certified in project management, design, bookkeeping and video editing. Available 24/7. Pay: $3/hour, but it's a great learning opportunity!\" (Wildest \"entry-level\" requirement you've seen? 👇)"}},
{"id":"d61-am","day":61,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Good morning to everyone just logging off a night shift 🌙 Before you rest, a gentle question: what's a work mistake that ended up teaching you something useful? A mixed-up time zone, a wrong attachment, a reply sent too fast? Mistakes can be great teachers, and sharing them helps newer VAs learn the easy way. Tell us yours below if you're comfortable, and be kind to each other's stories. #upskilling #nightshiftvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d61-noon","day":61,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Learning sticks when you use it fast. Try the 48-hour rule: within two days of finishing a lesson, use one idea from it on real work, then explain it to someone in three sentences. For example, after Inbox triage in 4 buckets in Executive Support Essentials, sort your next inbox into the four buckets and walk a fellow VA through them. If you can't explain it yet, go back to just that slide. Which lesson will you put to work this week? #circleacademy #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d61-hub","day":61,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Cebu VAs, did you work in an office before going freelance, maybe around IT Park or downtown? 🌊 What's one skill from that job that still helps you as a VA today? And what are you learning now that the office never taught you? Share both below so fellow Cebu VAs can swap ideas. #cebuvas #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d61-laughs","day":61,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: You finish a 12-module course in one weekend, download the certificate, update your profile, and Monday's first client message is 'Hey, since you're good with tech, can you fix my printer?'"}},
{"id":"d62-am","day":62,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"First-time wins deserve a spotlight! ✨ Did you use a brand-new skill on real client work this week? Maybe your first clean pivot table, your first meeting invite that got every time zone right, or the first status update your client actually praised. Tell us what you tried and how it went. Every \"I did it for real\" moment deserves a round of applause, so let's give it. 🎉 #circlewins #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d62-noon","day":62,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Practise the hard parts before they're real. After the Calming an upset client lesson in VA Foundations: Client Communication, try the matching Circle Bestie role-play, The 3AM angry client. You'll get scores for communication, technical skill and crisis handling, plus a few pointers for next time. Free members get 3 AI sessions a day. Run the same scenario a week later and compare your scores. Which client situation would you most like to rehearse? #circlebestie #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d62-hub","day":62,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Mount Apo views or Davao Gulf breezes? 🌄 If you could take a course anywhere around Davao, where would you set up your laptop, and what would you study there? Share your dream study setup, and your real one too. No judgment if it's the dining table. #davaovas #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d62-laughs","day":62,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"Certified course collector","items":["Certificate folder bigger than the client folder","Starts every sentence with 'So in the course they said…'","Buys a new notebook for every course, uses 3 pages","Progress bar stuck at 92% since forever","Signs up for 'Intro to Productivity' instead of being productive","Already eyeing the next course before finishing this one","What's in your course-collector pack? Add it below 👇"]}},
{"id":"d63-am","day":63,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"How do you fit learning around a night shift? 🌙 Some VAs study right after logging off, others save it for the afternoon once they've rested. There's no wrong rhythm, only the one that works for your body and your week. If you're still figuring it out, that's okay too. What time of day does learning actually stick for you? Let's swap routines in the comments. #nightshiftvas #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d63-noon","day":63,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Stuck between two outside certifications? Try this three-question check: 1) Can you practise the skill on real tasks within a month? 2) Will it help you raise your rate or add a new service? 3) Is the issuer easy to verify, with every fee listed upfront? If you get two \"yes\" answers, it's probably worth a closer look. Before you pay, book a Circle Mentor who works in that niche and ask what clients actually value. Which two are you deciding between? #certifications #vacareer","body":{}},
{"id":"d63-hub","day":63,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Baguio is known as a city of students, with schools and review centers all around town. 📚 Does that study energy rub off on you? Baguio VAs, tell us what you're learning this month and the one habit that keeps you consistent: a set study hour, a study buddy, or a planner you actually use? #baguiovas #upskilling","body":{}},
{"id":"d63-laughs","day":63,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"A VA signs up for a free webinar called 'Master Automation in 60 Minutes.' Minute 5: excited, taking neat notes. Minute 20: building a workflow so client emails send themselves. Minute 45: the workflow sends the same 'Quick update!' email to the client 14 times. Minute 60: the VA has definitely mastered something, just not automation. The profile now proudly lists a brand-new skill: 'Damage control.' Honestly, that one might pay better. Got an automation mishap of your own? Share it below."}},
{"id":"d64-am","day":64,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Work-life wins count too! ✨ Did you make it to a birthday, a school program or a long family lunch because you planned your shift around it? Or cook a real meal between calls and actually sit down to eat it? Tell us about one moment this week when home life and work fit together, even for an hour. Let's celebrate the balance wins. 💛 #homelife #circlewins","body":{}},
{"id":"d64-prompt","day":64,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"The strangest place I've ever gone to find one more bar of signal is…","body":{}},
{"id":"d64-noon","day":64,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Outage-proof your workday in four steps: 1) Keep a charged power bank or small UPS for your router. 2) Set up a mobile data backup and test it once a month. 3) Write a short 'power outage' message template so you can update clients in seconds. 4) Work from cloud-saved files so nothing is lost mid-task. Bonus: keep a flashlight where you can find it in the dark. What's in your outage kit? #outageready #remotework","body":{}},
{"id":"d64-hub","day":64,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Night-shift lounge check-in 🌙 Who's sharing the house with you while you work? A sleeping family, a roommate on a different schedule, or a gecko on the ceiling with a lot to say at 3am? How do you keep the peace (and the quiet)? Share your little household tricks. #nightshiftlounge #homelife","body":{}},
{"id":"d64-laughs","day":64,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":3,"timer":"00:47:12","caption":"Screenshot captured: a frozen 'Reconnecting…' screen, 14% battery, and a draft email that just says 'Hi, so sorry, the power is'","punchline":"The power was out for 47 minutes. That 3% activity? Just you, sitting in the dark, gently shaking the mouse to prove you were still emotionally present."}},
{"id":"d65-am","day":65,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Rest check after the shift 🌙 When your schedule runs opposite to the people you live with, how do you stay connected? A shared breakfast before you sleep, notes on the fridge, a weekend meal that's always protected? Share one small ritual that keeps you close to your household. And if the flipped schedule has been feeling lonely, Circle BFF can match you with a VA who has been through the same thing. #nightshiftvas #homelife","body":{}},
{"id":"d65-noon","day":65,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"No internet doesn't have to mean no work. Keep a short \"offline task list\" for the moments your connection drops: drafting replies, outlining tomorrow's to-do list, updating notes saved on your laptop, sorting files you've already downloaded. At the start of each shift, make the files you'll need most available offline, as long as your client's data rules allow it. Send your client a quick heads-up, then keep going offline. What's on your offline list? #remotework #vatips","body":{}},
{"id":"d65-hub","day":65,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"On the hottest Luzon afternoons, how do you keep your work corner (and your laptop) cool? ☀️ A fan aimed at the desk, a cooling pad, a move to the shadiest room in the house, or a cold drink always within reach? Share your best heat-beating setup so fellow Luzon VAs can borrow the idea. #luzonvas #homelife","body":{}},
{"id":"d65-laughs","day":65,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Client","text":"Can you hear me now?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Yes! Sorry, my internet just dropped. Go ahead."},{"who":"Client","text":"No worries. So, the most important part of this whole project is—"},{"who":"Me","text":"Hello? You froze. Hello??"},{"who":"Client","text":"—and that's basically everything. Any questions?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Just one. Could you repeat… all of it?"}]}},
{"id":"d66-am","day":66,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Small win, big smile: did your internet survive a full shift without a single drop this week? 🎉 Or maybe you finally got that backup power bank, a better chair, or a door that actually stays closed during calls. Home-setup upgrades deserve a celebration too. Show off your latest improvement in the comments! ✨ #circlewins #homeoffice","body":{}},
{"id":"d66-noon","day":66,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Scam-Buster note on 'free equipment' offers 🔎 A common fake job pattern: you're 'hired' very fast, told a company laptop is on the way, then asked to pay for shipping, insurance or a 'starter kit' first. Legitimate employers don't ask new hires to pay upfront to receive work equipment. If an offer comes with a fee and pressure to move the chat to an outside messaging app, pause and report it to Circle Scam-Buster. Seen a version of this one? Share the red flags you noticed. #scamawareness #staysafe","body":{}},
{"id":"d66-hub","day":66,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Surprise visitors! 🌊 When relatives come over from the next island for a long weekend, what happens to your work corner? Do you move the laptop to the bedroom, hang a 'meeting in progress' sign, or join the fun once you log off? Visayas VAs, share your houseguest game plan. #visayasvas #homelife","body":{}},
{"id":"d66-laughs","day":66,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"Working from home: a calm desk by the window, a quiet house, soft music, and a hot drink while you focus on deep work.","reality":"Working from home: a rooster that thinks 3pm is sunrise, someone asking you to 'just watch the rice for a second', the neighbor's renovation starting the moment you unmute, and a 'hot' drink that's been cold since your first meeting."}},
{"id":"d67-am","day":67,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Let's talk about boundaries at home. 🌙 When you work nights, family and friends might not always see it as 'real work', because you're home all day. That can feel lonely or frustrating. How have you explained your schedule to the people you live with? Any phrases or habits that helped them understand? Your answer might help someone having that exact conversation this week. #nightshiftvas #boundaries","body":{}},
{"id":"d67-noon","day":67,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Shared house, shared Wi-Fi? A few small tweaks can protect your work calls: ask the household to pause big downloads and streaming during your meeting hours, plug your laptop into the router with a cable if you can, and post a simple schedule on the fridge so everyone knows your 'quiet hours'. It's less about rules and more about teamwork. What's your household Wi-Fi agreement? #remotework #homeoffice","body":{}},
{"id":"d67-hub","day":67,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Who's the official family tech support in your house? 🌄 From the Bukidnon highlands to the coast, someone always ends up fixing the router, the TV and a relative's phone, sometimes on top of a full client shift. Is it you, Mindanao VAs? Share the funniest 'can you fix this?' request you've had this week. #mindanaovas #homelife","body":{}},
{"id":"d67-laughs","day":67,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"Your internet the day after you pay the bill","text":"Still moving at the speed of a sleepy snail, but now with a very cheerful 'Thank you for your payment!' text message."}},
{"id":"d68-am","day":68,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Gratitude break! 💛 Working from home comes with its share of chaos, but also some sweet perks: lunch with family, zero commute, comfy clothes on every shift, a window view you actually like. What's one home-life perk you're thankful for this week? Short answers welcome. Let's fill this thread with good vibes. ✨ #wfhperks #gratitude","body":{}},
{"id":"d68-noon","day":68,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Your workspace doesn't need to be a full room to feel like an office. A few low-cost ideas: a folding screen or curtain to mark your 'work zone', a small warm lamp for late shifts, a headset with a decent mic to cut background noise, and one basket where all your work stuff lives. Small boundaries make it easier to switch into work mode. What's your smartest space-saving trick? #homeoffice #vatips","body":{}},
{"id":"d68-hub","day":68,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Manila traffic or a cozy day at home? 🚗 On your off hours, do you still head out, or has EDSA convinced you that home is the best destination? Share your favorite stay-at-home reset after a long shift. Bonus points if it involves food. #manilavas #homelife","body":{}},
{"id":"d68-laughs","day":68,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: The power comes back, the whole street cheers, your router takes 11 minutes to remember who it is, and your phone lights up with 9 client messages, each one containing slightly more question marks than the last."}},
{"id":"d69-am","day":69,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Quiet question for the end of your shift: how are you doing, really? 🌙 Home life can be heavy sometimes: family needs, bills, noise, outages, all on top of work. If today felt like a lot, you're not alone in that. Tell us one thing that went okay today, however small. If you need more than a thread, Circle BFF and the Vent Room are open, Circle Wellness can point you to support, and if you're ever in crisis, please reach out to your local crisis line. #nightshiftvas #checkin","body":{}},
{"id":"d69-noon","day":69,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Family emergency in the middle of a shift? A plan you agreed on in advance makes it easier to step away without panic. Talk with your client early about how you'll flag an urgent absence, keep a short handover note with task status, and know which tasks can safely wait. A clear heads-up tends to land far better than silence. Do you have an 'emergency step-away' agreement with your clients? #clientcommunication #worklifebalance","body":{}},
{"id":"d69-hub","day":69,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"What's the soundtrack of your shift, Cebu? 🌊 Waves in the distance, jeepney horns on the main road, a karaoke session down the street, or just the fan humming beside you? Share the sounds of your workspace tonight. #cebuvas #homelife","body":{}},
{"id":"d69-laughs","day":69,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"Power outage survival mode: VA edition","items":["Laptop at 23%, deciding which tabs deserve to live","Phone flashlight now working as a ring light","Holds the phone hotspot up high like a trophy for one more bar","'Power outage' client message already drafted and saved","Recognizes the router's reboot lights like a heartbeat","Charging a power bank with another power bank","Fan stopped, so now fanning self with a printed invoice"]}},
{"id":"d70-am","day":70,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Meet the coworkers you never hired! 🐾 The cat who naps on your keyboard, the dog who barks the second you unmute, the little one who waves at every video call… Who keeps you company during your shift, and what's their official job title? Head of Snacks? Chief Keyboard Inspector? Introduce your coworkers in the comments. ✨ #wfhlife #homelife","body":{}},
{"id":"d70-noon","day":70,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Balancing family time and night shifts takes planning, not just willpower. Try blocking your week in a calendar app: work hours, sleep hours, and at least one protected family moment, like a shared meal or a weekend outing. Once it's written down, it's easier to protect, and easier for your family to see too. What's one family ritual you never miss? #worklifebalance #vatips","body":{}},
{"id":"d70-hub","day":70,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Davao VAs, family meals on a VA schedule can get creative 🌄 Do you join the family lunch before you sleep, eat your 'breakfast' while everyone else has dinner, or keep a plate (and some fresh fruit from the market) set aside for after your shift? Tell us how meal times work in your house. 😄 #davaovas #homelife","body":{}},
{"id":"d70-laughs","day":70,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"Halfway through a weekly client call, a VA is presenting a perfectly color-coded report. Background tidy, voice calm, everything on track. Then a tiny hand slides a crayon drawing in front of the webcam. Then a second drawing. Then a very serious little voice announces, 'This one is for the boss.' The VA braces for the worst. The client leans in, smiles, and holds up a drawing from their own kid. The meeting runs ten minutes over, and the notes now include one new action item: 'Frame the drawings.' Has a family member ever made a surprise cameo on your calls? Tell us in the comments."}},
{"id":"d71-am","day":71,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Think back to your very first week as a VA. 🌙 What did you worry about that seems small now? Maybe it was your first client call, your first invoice, or setting up the time tracker. Growth can be quiet, and it's easy to miss how far you've come. Share one thing that used to scare you and now feels normal. Someone just starting out will be glad to read it. #vajourney #growth","body":{}},
{"id":"d71-prompt","day":71,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"I knew I'd officially leveled up from newbie VA the day I…","body":{}},
{"id":"d71-noon","day":71,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Goals stick better when they're specific. Instead of 'get better clients', try 'add one new service and land one project with it by the end of next quarter'. Then list three small steps you can take this month. Circle Mentors can help you sanity-check your plan, and if your new service is executive support, the free Executive Support Essentials course in Circle Academy is a good place to start. What's one goal you'd write down today? #vagoals #growth","body":{}},
{"id":"d71-hub","day":71,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Picture the pine trees outside your window a year from now, Baguio VAs. 🌲 What's different? A new skill, a better rate, a dream client, a cozier setup? Share one goal you're quietly working toward. The fog might roll in thick some mornings, but your next step can still be clear. #baguiovas #vagoals","body":{}},
{"id":"d71-laughs","day":71,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":12,"timer":"00:14:09","caption":"Screenshot caught: a VA updating a long-time client's report template, frozen mid-scroll on their very first report for this client, two years old and in five different fonts.","punchline":"Activity: 12%. Cringe level: 100%. The numbers were right. The fonts were not. Growth is looking back at old work and wincing, kindly. What first-ever piece of work would you love to redo? Tell us below."}},
{"id":"d72-am","day":72,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Milestone alert! ✨ Did you hit a VA anniversary, land a long-term client, raise your rate, or finally send an invoice without overthinking it? Every step from newbie to seasoned deserves a moment in the spotlight. Tell us your latest milestone and how long it took to get there. 🎉 #milestones #circlewins","body":{}},
{"id":"d72-noon","day":72,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Growing your skills? Let your pricing grow too, starting with a rush rate 🎓 Decide what counts as a rush (same-day turnaround, a deadline under 24 hours), set a clear surcharge on top of your usual rate, and add it to your written agreement before you need it. Then, when an urgent request lands, you can reply calmly: 'Happy to! This falls under my rush rate, so here's the quote.' The client gets a choice, and your fast work gets valued. Do you charge a rush rate? How did you set it? #ratesmatter #vatips","body":{}},
{"id":"d72-hub","day":72,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Midnight reflection time in the lounge 🌙 What's one night-shift habit you've built that your newbie self would be proud of? Maybe a pre-shift checklist, a wind-down routine, or simply knowing when to log off. Share it so the newer night owls can borrow it. #nightshiftlounge #growth","body":{}},
{"id":"d72-laughs","day":72,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Client","text":"Any chance this could be ready by tomorrow morning?"},{"who":"Me (year 1)","text":"Yes!! Of course!! I'll stay up all night, no problem at all!! 😊"},{"who":"Me (year 3)","text":"Sure, if we move the weekly report to Thursday."},{"who":"Me (year 5)","text":"Happy to. That falls under my rush rate. Want me to send the quote?"},{"who":"Client","text":"Actually… Friday is fine."}]}},
{"id":"d73-am","day":73,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Growth isn't always a straight line, and that's okay. 🌙 Some months you'll level up fast, and some months just keeping steady is the achievement. Both count. What's one thing you're proud of handling this year that no certificate could ever show? Share it below, and give yourself a little credit while you're at it. #vajourney #growth","body":{}},
{"id":"d73-noon","day":73,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"As you grow, scammers notice. 🔎 Two patterns aimed at experienced VAs: someone offers to 'rent' your verified account or asks you to log in for them, so they can work under your name and rank; or a 'trial task' that turns out to be the whole project, unpaid, followed by silence. Your verified account is tied to your own ID, so never share your login or let anyone else use it. Keep test tasks small and agree in writing on whether they're paid. Check unusual offers in Circle Scam-Buster before you commit. Which pattern have you seen? #scamawareness #staysafe","body":{}},
{"id":"d73-hub","day":73,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Luzon VAs, time for a little look back. 🌾 Whether you work near the rice terraces or in the middle of the city, what's one goal you set as a newbie that you've already reached? Share it, then tell us the next one on your list. #luzonvas #vagoals","body":{}},
{"id":"d73-laughs","day":73,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"Seasoned VA life: calm mornings, an organized inbox, clients who respect your hours, and systems that basically run themselves.","reality":"Seasoned VA life: the same 3am ping, except now you reply in four words, finish it in six minutes, and invoice it in two. The chaos never left. You just got faster than it."}},
{"id":"d74-am","day":74,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Calling all comeback stories! 🎉 Maybe you lost a client and found a better one, failed a skills test and passed the retake, or started over after a long break. Growth often hides inside a tough moment. Share a bounce-back you're proud of, big or small. We're cheering already. ✨ #comebackstory #circlewins","body":{}},
{"id":"d74-noon","day":74,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Want to go from task-taker to trusted partner? Start suggesting improvements, not just finishing tasks. Once a month, send your client one short note: what you noticed, what you'd change, and how much time it could save. It shows initiative and can open the door to bigger projects. Start small, with one process you already know well. What improvement could you propose this week? #vagrowth #clientrelations","body":{}},
{"id":"d74-hub","day":74,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"If your VA career were an island-hopping trip across the Visayas, where would you be right now? 🌊 Just leaving port, halfway across the strait, or already relaxing on the beach? Share where you are and which island you're sailing to next. #visayasvas #vagoals","body":{}},
{"id":"d74-laughs","day":74,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"Seasoned VAs booking a 30-minute task","text":"Blocks 45 minutes: 30 for the task, 10 for the login that suddenly needs a new code, and 5 to find the file the client swears they already shared."}},
{"id":"d75-am","day":75,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Wherever you are in your VA journey, you belong here. 🌙 Newbies, you're braver than you think. Seasoned VAs, your experience is a gift to someone just starting. So let's connect the two: if you're new, ask one question you've been too shy to ask. If you've been doing this a while, answer one. This thread is a safe space for both. #vacommunity #growth","body":{}},
{"id":"d75-noon","day":75,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Make a 'brag file' this week. It's a simple document where you record wins as they happen: a kind note from a client, a process you improved, a deadline you saved, a new skill you learned. When it's time to update your profile, raise your rate, or apply through Circle Jobs, you'll have real examples ready instead of trying to remember. What's the first thing you'd put in yours? #vagrowth #careertips","body":{}},
{"id":"d75-hub","day":75,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Rafters on the Cagayan de Oro River learn to read the water before they reach the rapids. 🌄 Mindanao VAs, what's one early warning sign you've learned to read on the job? A vague brief, a sudden change in a client's tone, a deadline that keeps moving? Share how you spot it, so newer VAs can learn to read the water too. #mindanaovas #vagrowth","body":{}},
{"id":"d75-laughs","day":75,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: Someone new in Circle Chat asks 'How do I handle a client who messages at 3am?' and you realize you've finally become the person with the answer… which you are typing at 3am."}},
{"id":"d76-am","day":76,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Tiny wins count too ✨ Let's measure how far you've come. Pick one task you do all the time: an inbox cleanup, a weekly report, a calendar reshuffle. How long did it take you the very first time, and how long does it take now? Share your 'then vs now' times below. Every minute you've shaved off is growth, and it deserves a cheer! #vawins #growthjourney","body":{}},
{"id":"d76-noon","day":76,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Calm in a client crisis is a skill, not a personality trait 🎓 and you can practise it before a real 3am emergency arrives. Try a role-play in Circle Bestie: pick a scenario like 'The 3AM angry client' or 'Store checkout is down', reply the way you would for real, then read your scores for communication, technical and crisis handling. Run the same scenario again a week later and compare. Tier 1 includes 3 free AI sessions a day, and Tier 2 is unlimited. Which scenario would you try first? Share how it went! #vaskills #crisisready","body":{}},
{"id":"d76-hub","day":76,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"From Makati condos to quiet streets in Marikina, Manila VAs have come a long way 🌏 What's one thing you used to do for free as a newbie that's now part of your paid scope? Rush jobs, extra revisions, weekend check-ins? Tell us how you made the switch, so newer VAs in the hub can learn from it. #manilavas #vagrowth","body":{}},
{"id":"d76-laughs","day":76,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"Brand-new VA, week one","items":["Converts the client's time zone on a calculator, then checks it twice","Sets four alarms for a 10am call","Screenshots every client message 'just in case'","Opens the client's shared drive like it might explode","Asks 'Sorry, is this a silly question?' before every question","Retakes the profile photo 19 times, then uses the first one","Celebrates the first invoice like a graduation"]}},
{"id":"d77-am","day":77,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Good morning, night owls 🌙 As your shift winds down, here's a gentle one for growth week: what's one choice your past self made that today's you is grateful for? Saying yes to that first client, saying no to a bad one, building a sleep routine, or simply not giving up during a hard week? Share it below, and send your past self a little thank-you while you're at it. Then rest well. #nightshiftvas #growth","body":{}},
{"id":"d77-noon","day":77,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Kind words from a client are worth more when you can share them 🎓 When a client says something like 'This is exactly what I needed', thank them, then ask: 'Would you be happy for me to quote that on my profile?' Get the yes in writing, and use only their first name or role if they prefer. Never edit their words or add details they didn't say. Over time, real reviews show new clients what working with you is like. Have you ever asked a client for a review? How did you word it? #vaskills #careergrowth","body":{}},
{"id":"d77-hub","day":77,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Canyoneering at Kawasan Falls often starts with one nervous first jump 🌊 Cebu VAs, what was the biggest leap of your VA career so far? Your first overseas client, leaving an office job, taking on a whole new type of work? Tell us what helped you jump, so someone standing on the ledge tonight can borrow your courage. #cebuvas #vagrowth","body":{}},
{"id":"d77-laughs","day":77,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"In their first week, a VA gets a message: 'Can you do a quick task?' They clear the whole evening, make a checklist, watch three tutorials and finish at 2am. Six months later, the same message arrives. The seasoned VA replies: 'Sure! Could you share the scope, the deadline and how many revisions you expect?' The client goes quiet for an hour, then sends a 14-step document titled 'Quick task (small)'. Growth isn't avoiding the quick task. It's asking questions before it eats your weekend. What's the longest 'quick task' you've ever seen? Tell us below."}},
{"id":"d78-am","day":78,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Shout-out time! 🙌 This week is all about community, so let's celebrate the people who helped you grow. Did someone answer your question in Circle Chat, look over your portfolio, or pass you a lead when you really needed it? Tell us what they did and how it helped. A little gratitude makes the whole Circle stronger. #gratitude #vacommunity","body":{}},
{"id":"d78-prompt","day":78,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"You know you've become the VA mentor in your friend group when…","body":{}},
{"id":"d78-noon","day":78,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Mentoring tip: the best questions are specific 🎓 Instead of \"How do I get clients?\", try \"I've sent ten proposals for admin roles with no replies. Could you look at this one and tell me the first thing you'd change?\" Specific questions get faster, more useful answers, and they respect your mentor's time. Circle Mentors is a great place to put this into practice. What question would you ask a mentor this week? Share it below. #vamentoring #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d78-hub","day":78,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Sharing is part of life in Davao, whether it's a bag of fresh fruit from the market or a good job lead 🌄 How do you give back to the VA community? Maybe you helped a neighbor set up their first profile, or showed a friend how to spot a fake job post. Share your story, or one way you'd like to help newer VAs this month! #davaovas #givingback","body":{}},
{"id":"d78-laughs","day":78,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":97,"timer":"01:03:45","caption":"Screenshot caught: a free mentoring call with a brand-new VA, timed on the personal tracker out of pure habit, mid-slide titled 'Why we never say yes to a quick task'","punchline":"Highest activity score of the week, on the one hour nobody is paying for. The time tracker would like to know who the client is. What's the most unexpected thing your tracker has ever caught? Share it below."}},
{"id":"d79-am","day":79,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"How did your shift go? 🌙 Before you rest, here's a softer question for community week: if a brand-new VA joined the Circle tonight, what's one thing you'd say to help them feel at home? A practical tip, a kind word, a reminder that everyone starts somewhere? Leave it below. And if you ARE new and still finding your people, say hi. We'll make room for you. #nightshiftvas #welcome","body":{}},
{"id":"d79-noon","day":79,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Giving back can be as simple as sharing a checklist 🎓 If you've found a smooth way to onboard a new client, clear an inbox or prep for a Monday call, write it as five to seven clear steps. Remove any client names or private details first. Then post it as a tip on the Feed or in your hub. If you're ranked Proven VA or higher and on Tier 2, it could even grow into a mentor module on Circle Mentors. Your 'obvious' process could save a newer VA hours. What checklist could you share this week? #vatips #givingback","body":{}},
{"id":"d79-hub","day":79,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Cool Baguio evenings are made for long talks over something warm ☕ Here's a twist on mentoring: what's something a newer VA, a younger cousin or a fresh graduate has taught YOU? A shortcut, a tool, a fresh way of thinking? Share it below, strawberry taho or hot chocolate in hand! #baguiovas #mentoring","body":{}},
{"id":"d79-laughs","day":79,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Newbie","text":"How do you always sound so calm in client messages?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Years of experience."},{"who":"Newbie","text":"Wow. So you don't panic anymore?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Oh, I panic. I just do it in the drafts folder."},{"who":"Newbie","text":"What's in your drafts folder?"},{"who":"Me","text":"Forty-seven versions of 'No worries at all! 😊'"}]}},
{"id":"d80-am","day":80,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Helpers, this one's for you! ✨ Did you lend a hand this week? Maybe you answered a question in a hub, recommended a fellow VA for a gig, or reminded a friend to take a real break. Those moments matter just as much as any new contract. Share one small act of giving back you did, or one you received. Let's fill the feed with good energy! #kindness #vacommunity","body":{}},
{"id":"d80-noon","day":80,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Not every \"mentor\" is a mentor 🔎 A common pattern: someone offers to coach you for free, builds trust over a few chats, then asks for a \"training fee\" to unlock a guaranteed job, or pushes you to move the conversation to an outside messaging app. Real mentors don't guarantee jobs and never need your ID or bank details. Keep conversations in Circle Chat, use Circle Mentors, and report anything odd to Circle Scam-Buster. Have you seen this pattern? Share what to watch for. #scamaware #staysafe","body":{}},
{"id":"d80-hub","day":80,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Pre-shift check-in for the lounge 🌙 Night shift can feel lonely, so let's keep each other company. What's one small thing you do to support a fellow night-shift VA? A quick \"you okay?\" message, a playlist share, a reminder to drink water? Share yours. And if tonight feels heavy, Circle BFF and the Vent Room are always open. #nightshiftvas #community","body":{}},
{"id":"d80-laughs","day":80,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"Recommending a VA friend to your client: they get hired, and you get to feel like a very proud talent scout.","reality":"They get hired, they're brilliant, and now your own client keeps asking, 'Could you set it up the way your friend does?'"}},
{"id":"d81-am","day":81,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Rise and rest, everyone 🌙 Here's a question to carry into your sleep: what's one thing you know now that you'd happily teach someone for free? It might be calendar management, handling a tricky client email, or simply protecting your rest on night shift. Share it below as a tip. Someone in the Circle might be looking for exactly that, and your hub is a lovely place to keep the conversation going. #nightshiftvas #givingback","body":{}},
{"id":"d81-noon","day":81,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Thinking about reviewing a fellow VA's portfolio or proposal? 🎓 Try the 'keep, change, cheer' method: start with one specific thing that works, then one clear change that would help most, and finish with encouragement. Keep it about the work, not the person. One focused suggestion beats ten vague ones. Want an experienced eye on your own work? You can book a session on Circle Mentors. Who's up for a portfolio swap in the comments? Remove any client details first! #vafeedback #mentoring","body":{}},
{"id":"d81-hub","day":81,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Rainy season or not, Luzon VAs always find a way to show up 🌧️ When a friend or cousin asks how to become a VA, what's the one warning you always give them? A scam red flag, a pricing mistake, a reminder to protect their sleep? Share it below so newer VAs can learn it too! #luzonvas #payitforward","body":{}},
{"id":"d81-laughs","day":81,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"Senior VAs when a newbie asks one tiny question","text":"Here's a 12-step guide, three templates, a checklist, my favorite keyboard shortcuts, a backup plan for power outages and a pep talk. Also, please drink some water."}},
{"id":"d82-am","day":82,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Mentors, mentees and everyone in between, let's celebrate! 🎉 Did you finish a session in Circle Mentors, help someone land their first gig, or finally ask for advice you'd been nervous to ask? Every step counts. Share your mentoring win this week, big or tiny, and leave a cheer on someone else's in the replies. #mentoring #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d82-noon","day":82,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Want to grow faster? Start a three-person accountability circle 🎓 Pick a shared goal (finishing a Circle Academy course, applying to jobs each week, building a portfolio), then check in weekly: one post in your hub, with each person replying with one win, one blocker and one next step. Rotate who starts the post. Prefer one-on-one? Pair up with a connection in Circle Chat instead. It's mentoring without the pressure of being 'the expert'. Who wants to form a group? Comment your goal and time zone below. #accountability #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d82-hub","day":82,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Islands are connected by boats, and Visayas VAs are connected by this hub 🌊 When the power goes out, community really shows. Has a neighbor, friend or fellow VA ever saved your shift during an outage? A borrowed power bank, a shared hotspot, a seat at a table near a generator? Share your story, and tell us how you returned the favor! #visayasvas #community","body":{}},
{"id":"d82-laughs","day":82,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: you volunteer to explain the time tracker to a newbie, share your screen, and realize it just captured your 23 open tabs, a tower of snack wrappers and a half-written email titled 'GENTLE invoice follow-up (3rd)'. What's your best screen-share save? Tell us below."}},
{"id":"d83-am","day":83,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Sunrise thought for the Circle 🌙 Communities grow when people feel safe asking \"silly\" questions. What's a question you were once nervous to ask as a VA that turned out to be totally normal? Share it so newer members know they're not alone, and so we can all smile at how far everyone has come. Sleep well after your shift! #nightshiftvas #nosillyquestions","body":{}},
{"id":"d83-noon","day":83,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Referring a fellow VA is one of the kindest things you can do, and it's a skill 🎓 Before you recommend someone, check three things: Have you seen their work? Do their skills match the role? Are they available? Then make a warm intro: one line about the need, one line about why they fit. Good referrals protect your reputation and theirs. Have you ever passed a lead along on Circle Jobs? Share how you did it. #referrals #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d83-hub","day":83,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"mindanao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"From the mountains to the coast, Mindanao VAs know how to show up for each other 🌄 What would you love this hub to do together? A skills-swap night, a newbie Q&A, a weekend check-in thread? Share your ideas and let's build it as a community! #mindanaovas #community","body":{}},
{"id":"d83-laughs","day":83,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"starter","text":"","body":{"title":"VA mentor starter pack","items":["Starts every answer with 'Great question! So…'","Has explained scope creep with a pizza analogy 200 times","Says 'you've got this!' at 3am with full conviction","Calls every mistake 'a learning moment', especially their own","Cheers louder for a mentee's first invoice than for their own","Still searches things they told the newbie were 'easy'","Owns a mug that says 'Have you checked the time zone?'"]}},
{"id":"d84-am","day":84,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Paying it forward starts small 🤝 As community week wraps up, let's each make one pledge for the week ahead. Answer a question in a hub, review someone's portfolio, pass a lead along on Circle Jobs, or check in on a friend who's been quiet lately. Write your pledge in the comments, and let's cheer each other on as we keep them. #payitforward #vacommunity","body":{}},
{"id":"d84-noon","day":84,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Boundaries make generosity last 🎓 Try a simple 'helping budget': choose how much time you can offer each week, like one hour, and a format that suits you, like answering questions in your hub or reviewing one member's draft. Save your best answers as templates so you can reuse them. Helping others shouldn't cost you your rest. How much time do you set aside to help others? Share your system below. #boundaries #mentoring","body":{}},
{"id":"d84-hub","day":84,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"manila-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Manila VAs, let's run a 'teach one, learn one' swap right here in the hub 🌏 Reply with one skill you could explain in a few lines (a spreadsheet shortcut, a client email trick, a calendar hack) and one thing you'd love to learn. Spot a match? Answer each other in the replies, no traffic required! #manilavas #skillshare","body":{}},
{"id":"d84-laughs","day":84,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"story","text":"","body":{"text":"A VA shares a tiny tip in the hub: 'Start every file name with the date, so everything sorts itself.' Five replies. Then forty. Someone makes a color-coded version. Someone else turns it into a checklist. By Friday the tip has its own nickname, 'The Date Thing', and three newbies have reorganized their whole drive. Feeling proud, the VA opens their own downloads folder: 312 files named 'Untitled', 'scan (4)' and 'NEW NEW'. They close the folder, open it again, and quietly start renaming. What's a tip you share all the time but secretly don't follow yourself? Tell us below."}},
{"id":"d85-am","day":85,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"We're almost at 90 days together in the Circle 🌙 Whether you joined on day one or just this morning after your shift, we're so glad you're here. Let's take a quiet moment: what's one thing that has changed for you since you joined? A new skill, a new friend, a calmer way to start your mornings? Share it below, and rest well knowing you're part of something good. #circle90days #nightshiftvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d85-prompt","day":85,"time":"09:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"laughs_prompt","format":"","text":"If my last 90 days as a VA were a movie, the title would be…","body":{}},
{"id":"d85-noon","day":85,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Our 90-day milestone is almost here, which makes this a perfect time for a mini career review 🎓 Grab a notebook or spreadsheet and answer four questions: What did I learn? What brought the most value to my clients? What drained me? What's my one focus for the next 90 days? If a skill gap shows up, check Circle Academy's free courses (client communication, scam-proof freelancing, executive support) or book a mentor on Circle Mentors to plan your next step. What's your focus? Share it so the Circle can cheer you on! #circle90days #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d85-hub","day":85,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"cebu-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"The Circle is almost 90 days old, Cebu VAs! 🌊 If we threw a milestone party on the island, what would be on the table? Lechon, dried mangoes, something sweet? And what's one thing from your past 90 days you'd cheer for? Share below! #cebuvas #circle90days","body":{}},
{"id":"d85-laughs","day":85,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"tracker","text":"","body":{"activity":4,"timer":"02:59:58","caption":"A slice of 90-day celebration cake, a party popper mid-pop, and a blurry hand reaching for the pause button one second too late","punchline":"Ninety days of focus, undone by a single slice of cake. The time tracker never forgets. It also never gets any cake. What's the worst-timed screenshot you've ever had? Tell us below."}},
{"id":"d86-am","day":86,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Let's throw a little party! 🎉 We're celebrating 90 days of VAs supporting VAs, and we want to hear YOUR highlights. What's your favorite moment so far? A win you shared, a laugh in Circle Laughs, a tip that saved your week? Drop it in the comments. Bonus points for emojis! #circle90days #vawins","body":{}},
{"id":"d86-noon","day":86,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Your profile deserves a 90-day glow-up 🎓 Clients search Circle Talent for verified VAs, so make yours easy to find: list your top three services first, use the plain words a client would type (like 'inbox management' or 'calendar scheduling'), and finish a Circle Academy course so its certificate shows on your profile. Been a VA for years? You can submit proof of work through Circle Verified for a higher rank. What's one thing you'll update on your profile this week? Tell us below! #profiletips #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d86-hub","day":86,"time":"18:00","host":"summit","channel":"hub","hub":"davao-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"The Circle is nearly 90 days old, and Davao VAs have been part of it from the start 🌄 If you could show a VA from the other side of the world one thing about working from Davao, what would it be? The view of the gulf, the fruit stand down the street, the calm early mornings? Share it below and give a neighbor's answer some love! #davaovas #circle90days","body":{}},
{"id":"d86-laughs","day":86,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"dialog","text":"","body":{"lines":[{"who":"Client","text":"Happy 90 days of working together! I got you something."},{"who":"Me","text":"Aww, really? What is it?"},{"who":"Client","text":"I added your time zone to my calendar."},{"who":"Me","text":"That's so thoughtful! So no more 3am messages?"},{"who":"Client","text":"Now I'll know exactly how late it is when I send them."}]}},
{"id":"d87-am","day":87,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Quiet victories deserve a spotlight too 🌙 As we near our 90-day milestone, let's honor the wins nobody else sees. Maybe you stayed calm during a 3am ping, finally settled into a sleep routine, or reached out in the Vent Room when you needed support. Which quiet victory are you proudest of? Share it below, gently and proudly. #circle90days #nightshiftvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d87-noon","day":87,"time":"12:00","host":"shield","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Celebrations attract scammers too 🔎 Around milestones like our 90 days, watch for messages promising \"anniversary prizes\" or \"loyalty bonuses\" that ask for a processing fee, a photo of your ID, a one-time code, or payment in crypto. A genuine giveaway never needs your password or money upfront. If a message claims to be from the Circle but feels off, don't click or reply. Report it through Circle Scam-Buster. Which red flags do you check first? Share them to help others. #scamaware #staysafe","body":{}},
{"id":"d87-hub","day":87,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"baguio-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Baguio VAs, pull on a jacket, because the Circle is almost 90 days old! 🌲 Here's a milestone twist: write a one-line note to the you who will scroll past this thread 90 days from now. What do you hope they've learned, built or finally let go of? Share your note below, and let's look back on them together next season. #baguiovas #circle90days","body":{}},
{"id":"d87-laughs","day":87,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"expectation","text":"","body":{"expectation":"First week as a VA: 'In 90 days I'll be calm, organized and fully booked, with inbox zero every Friday.'","reality":"Day 90: fully booked, mostly calm, 1,482 unread emails and a sticky note that just says 'ASK ABOUT INVOICE???' in three colors."}},
{"id":"d88-am","day":88,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"What a three months it's been ✨ Not every lesson arrives as a win. What's one thing the past 90 days taught you the hard way? A scope you'll define earlier, a boundary you'll set sooner, a red flag you now spot in seconds? Share it below so someone else can learn it the easy way. #circle90days #lessonslearned","body":{}},
{"id":"d88-noon","day":88,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Here's a 90-day question worth asking: has your role quietly grown while your agreement stayed the same? 🎓 Open your original scope and list what you actually do now. Sort each new task into one of three groups: add it to your written scope (and your rate), swap it for something else, or quote it separately. Then share the list with your client as a short, friendly update. Want to rehearse the money part first? Try the 'Unpaid extra work' role-play in Circle Bestie. How much has your role changed since you started? #scopecheck #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d88-hub","day":88,"time":"18:00","host":"luna","channel":"hub","hub":"night-shift-lounge","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Evening, night-shift crew 🌙 For almost 90 days, this lounge has been a place to start the workday together while much of the city winds down. What's your favorite part of your night-shift routine now? A pre-shift snack, a playlist, that quiet 4am calm? Share it below, and here's to many more nights together. #nightshiftvas #circle90days","body":{}},
{"id":"d88-laughs","day":88,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"nobody","text":"","body":{"who":"Me, 90 days into saying 'Noted'","text":"Noted. Noted! Noted 🙂. Noted, thank you. Duly noted. Noted with love. Noted (internally screaming). N0ted. Noted."}},
{"id":"d89-am","day":89,"time":"07:30","host":"luna","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Just one sunrise away from our 90-day milestone 🌙 Thank you for every shift you've shown up for and every kind word you've shared here. As we look ahead, what do you hope the Circle becomes in the next 90 days? More hubs, more mentoring, more laughs? Tell us your wish below, then get some well-earned rest. #circle90days #nightshiftvas","body":{}},
{"id":"d89-noon","day":89,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Before the 90-day celebrations end, send each client a short 'quarter in review' 🎓 Keep it to five lines: the main tasks you've handled, one result you're proud of (hours saved, a process fixed, a deadline rescued), one thing you've learned about how they like to work, one idea for the next quarter, and a thank-you. It reminds clients of value they might not see day to day, and it can open the door to bigger work. What would go in your quarter in review? Share a line below! #quarterreview #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d89-hub","day":89,"time":"18:00","host":"aurora","channel":"hub","hub":"luzon-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Thank you, Luzon VAs, from Ilocos to Bicol, for making this hub feel like home 🌏 As the Circle reaches 90 days, what's one conversation, tip or laugh from this hub that stuck with you? Share it below, and give a warm welcome to any new faces joining the celebration! #luzonvas #circle90days","body":{}},
{"id":"d89-laughs","day":89,"time":"21:00","host":"punchline","channel":"laughs","hub":"","kind":"meme","format":"pov","text":"","body":{"text":"POV: it's day 90 and you scroll back to your very first post in the Circle: 'Hi, sorry, is it okay to ask a question here?' Now you're the one answering questions, and you still open every reply with 'Sorry if this is obvious, but…' Who else has come full circle? 👇"}},
{"id":"d90-am","day":90,"time":"07:30","host":"glow","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"post","format":"","text":"Happy 90 days, Circle! 🎉✨ Today we celebrate every VA who joined, shared, asked, laughed and helped someone else rise. Thank you for building a community that's verified, kind and looking out for each other. Now it's your turn: describe your Circle experience in exactly three words. Ready, set, comment! #circle90days #vacommunity","body":{}},
{"id":"d90-noon","day":90,"time":"12:00","host":"sage","channel":"feed","hub":"","kind":"tip","format":"","text":"Day 90 is a great finish line and an even better starting line 🎓 For the next 90 days, try the 1-1-1 plan: one skill to learn (a free Circle Academy course like Executive Support Essentials, or a practice round in Circle Bestie), one habit to build (like a weekly review every Friday), and one connection to make (book a mentor on Circle Mentors, or find an accountability buddy in your hub). Write all three somewhere you'll see every day. What's your 1-1-1? Share it in the comments! #nextchapter #vaskills","body":{}},
{"id":"d90-hub","day":90,"time":"18:00","host":"coral","channel":"hub","hub":"visayas-vas","kind":"question","format":"","text":"Ninety days, many islands, one hub 🌊 Visayas VAs, the Circle celebrates its 90th day today! If our milestone were a beach day, what would you bring: snacks, a speaker, a good book, or your laptop \"just in case\"? Share below, and tell us one thing you're excited about next! #visayasvas #circle90days","body":{}},
